1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,248
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:05,665 --> 00:00:09,923
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسليمًا كَثِيرًا

3
00:00:12,002 --> 00:00:16,357
The virtues of encouraging Jihad(جهاد), At-Tahreez(ألتحريض).

4
00:00:18,859 --> 00:00:20,284
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

5
00:00:20,484 --> 00:00:26,273
فَقاتِل في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ لا تُكَلَّفُ إِلّا نَفسَكَ ۚ

6
00:00:26,632 --> 00:00:29,948
وَحَرِّضِ المُؤمِنينَ ۖ

7
00:00:30,348 --> 00:00:43,893
عَسَى اللَّهُ أَن يَكُفَّ بَأسَ الَّذينَ كَفَروا ۚ وَاللَّهُ أَشَدُّ بَأسًا وَأَشَدُّ تَنكيلًا۞

8
00:00:44,393 --> 00:00:48,878
So fight O Muhammadﷺ in the cause of Allah.

9
00:00:50,022 --> 00:00:52,538
You are not held responsible except for yourself,

10
00:00:53,965 --> 00:01:00,408
and encourage the believers to join you, that Perhaps Allah will restrain the might of those who disbelieved,

11
00:01:01,058 --> 00:01:03,996
and Allah is greater in might and stronger in punishment.

12
00:01:04,842 --> 00:01:07,233
This is an An-Nisa(ألنساء) Verse 84.

13
00:01:09,862 --> 00:01:12,603
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is giving an order to Muhammadﷺ to fight,

14
00:01:14,111 --> 00:01:18,607
and then Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is saying that as long as you are making Tahreez(تحريض), you're encouraging others to fight,

15
00:01:18,646 --> 00:01:24,212
it doesn't matter if they do go or not as long as you are doing with Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ wants you to do.

16
00:01:25,763 --> 00:01:29,123
And I think this is also a reflection of the meaning,

17
00:01:29,155 --> 00:01:32,868
لَا يَضُرُّهُمْ مَنْ خَلَفَهُمْ

18
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:35,577
In the Hadith(حديث) of Taifah Al-Mansura(طائفة المنصورة), it says that

19
00:01:35,653 --> 00:01:38,344
they are not harmed by the ones, who don't go along with it.

20
00:01:39,175 --> 00:01:46,541
Doesn't really hinder their progress in their path towards Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, they're going to carry on doing it.

21
00:01:47,975 --> 00:01:51,986
Regardless of who is coming along and who is not.

22
00:01:55,021 --> 00:01:56,717
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ also says:

23
00:01:56,817 --> 00:02:04,715
يا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ حَرِّضِ المُؤمِنينَ عَلَى القِتالِ ۚ

24
00:02:05,115 --> 00:02:12,550
إن يَكُن مِنكُم عِشرونَ صابِرونَ يَغلِبوا مِائَتَينِ ۚ

25
00:02:12,950 --> 00:02:22,710
وَإِن يَكُن مِنكُم مِائَةٌ يَغلِبوا أَلفًا مِنَ الَّذينَ كَفَروا

26
00:02:23,385 --> 00:02:30,137
مِنَ الَّذينَ كَفَروا بِأَنَّهُم قَومٌ لا يَفقَهونَ۞

27
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:33,384
O Prophet urged the believers to do battle.

28
00:02:33,829 --> 00:02:40,007
if they are among you 20 steadfast, they will overcome 200,

29
00:02:40,507 --> 00:02:47,597
and if they are among you 100 steadfast, they will overcome 1000 of those who have disbelieved,

30
00:02:47,897 --> 00:02:50,678
because they are people who do not understand.

31
00:02:51,244 --> 00:02:53,709
This is in Al-Anfal(ألأنفال) Verse 65.

32
00:02:54,409 --> 00:02:55,209
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

33
00:02:55,272 --> 00:02:57,913
يَٰأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِىُّ حَرِّضِ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَى ٱلْقِتَالِ ۚ

34
00:02:58,255 --> 00:03:12,257
إِن يَكُن مِّنكُمْ عِشْرُونَ صَٰبِرُونَ يَغْلِبُواْ مِاْئَتَيْنِ ۚ وَإِن يَكُن مِّنكُم مِّاْئَةٌ يَغْلِبُوٓاْ أَلْفًا مِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُونَ۞

35
00:03:17,894 --> 00:03:23,756
The author says, we will end this chapter, so he's talking about the chapter of Tahreez(تحريض).

36
00:03:25,829 --> 00:03:29,863
He says we will end this chapter with the famous story of Umm Ibrahim(أمِّ اِبْراهِيْم).

37
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:35,694
This story was mentioned by scholars like Abu Jafar Al-Luban(أبوجعفرألبان),

38
00:03:36,347 --> 00:03:45,939
he narrates it is mentioned that one of the righteous woman in Basra(بصرى), was Umm-Ibrahim Al-Hashimiya(أم إبراهيم ألهاشمية).

39
00:03:47,874 --> 00:03:52,746
The enemy attacked one of the Muslim towns, so people were encouraged to join Jihad(جهاد).

40
00:03:54,346 --> 00:03:58,831
Abdul Wahid Bin Zaid Al-Basri(عبدالواحدبن زيد ألبصري) delivered a speech, encouraging Jihad(جهاد).

41
00:03:59,605 --> 00:04:02,547
And among the audience was Umm Ibrahim(أمِّ اِبْراهِيْم).

42
00:04:04,790 --> 00:04:08,764
Among the things that Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد) talked about was Al-Hoor(ألحور), the woman of paradise.

43
00:04:09,464 --> 00:04:13,740
So here we have Abdul Wahid Bin Zaid(عبدالواحدبن زيد) is delivering a speech,

44
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:20,690
encouraging, whoever is there to participate in Ghazoo(غزؤ).

45
00:04:21,815 --> 00:04:26,918
And it's happened that her name is Umm-Ibrahim Al-Hashimiya(أم إبراهيم ألهاشمية),

46
00:04:27,172 --> 00:04:32,518
Hashmiyyah(هاشمية) from Banu Hashim(بنوهاشم), she was attending, in that session.

47
00:04:34,718 --> 00:04:37,125
And he went on and on describing on Hoor-Ul-Ain(حورالعين).

48
00:04:37,225 --> 00:04:42,071
Now I didn't translate everything he said, because a lot of it was poetry.

49
00:04:44,514 --> 00:04:47,213
But there was a lot of things that he had to say about Al-Hoor(ألحور).

50
00:04:48,265 --> 00:04:53,604
So Umm-Ibrahim(أم إبراهيم) heard that she stood up and said to Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد):

51
00:04:54,004 --> 00:04:55,348
You know my son Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم),

52
00:04:56,014 --> 00:05:00,112
and you know that the nobility of Al-Basra(ألبصرى) wish to have him marry one of their daughters,

53
00:05:00,736 --> 00:05:02,880
and I have not yet to agreed to any one of them.

54
00:05:04,209 --> 00:05:08,048
But I like this girl you described, and I would be happy to marry her to my son.

55
00:05:08,677 --> 00:05:10,103
Can you please describe her again.!

56
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:16,390
So Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد) goes and brings now new description,

57
00:05:16,448 --> 00:05:18,248
he doesn't use the old description that he had.

58
00:05:18,319 --> 00:05:24,562
He had total new package present to her now, and the description of this Hooriya(حورية).

59
00:05:27,031 --> 00:05:28,139
 Umm-Ibrahim(أم إبراهيم) said:

60
00:05:28,439 --> 00:05:36,938
I want my son to marry this girl, and I would pay you 10,000 dinars, as her dowry, the dinar(دينار) is the golden coin.

61
00:05:37,802 --> 00:05:42,592
So it's more than the Dirham(درهم), Dirham(درهم) is usually silver and dinar(دينار) is gold.

62
00:05:46,212 --> 00:05:49,740
As her dowry and you take him with you in this army.

63
00:05:50,906 --> 00:05:55,056
He might die as a Shaheed(شَهِيد), and intercede for me on the day of judgment.

64
00:05:55,542 --> 00:05:58,944
And you don't have to write down the whole story. I'll give you the notes for that.

65
00:06:01,455 --> 00:06:07,547
If you do so, Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد) told her: If you do so that is a great success for you and your son.

66
00:06:08,858 --> 00:06:13,097
She then called her son from the audience, so Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was there so she called him up.

67
00:06:13,722 --> 00:06:14,437
She said: Stand up!

68
00:06:14,942 --> 00:06:16,602
So he stood up and said: Yes, my mother!

69
00:06:17,147 --> 00:06:20,936
She said: Are you pleased to marry this girl with the condition of giving your soul to Allah.?

70
00:06:22,285 --> 00:06:25,678
إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱشْتَرَىٰ مِنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَنفُسَهُمْ وَأَمْوَٰلَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ ٱلْجَنَّةَ

71
00:06:26,925 --> 00:06:28,309
So Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) said: Yes!

72
00:06:28,509 --> 00:06:29,492
I am very pleased.

73
00:06:30,096 --> 00:06:32,441
She said: Oh Allah, you are my witness

74
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:39,490
that I have married my son to this girl from paradise, with the condition, he spends his soul in Your sake.

75
00:06:40,851 --> 00:06:44,920
So the witnesses is Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ of this contract of marriage.

76
00:06:48,473 --> 00:06:53,823
Then she went and brought back with her, 10,000 dinars, and gave it to Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد) and said:

77
00:06:54,183 --> 00:06:58,761
This is her dowry, take it and use it to provide for the Mujahideen(مجاهدين).

78
00:06:59,637 --> 00:07:02,716
She then purchased for her son, a good horse and she armed him.

79
00:07:03,247 --> 00:07:09,863
When the army started its March Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) came out with the reciters of Qur'an surrounding him, and they were reciting.

80
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:16,615
Indeed, Allah has purchased from the believers their lives and their properties in exchange for that they will have paradise.

81
00:07:17,048 --> 00:07:21,324
إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱشْتَرَىٰ مِنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَنفُسَهُمْ وَأَمْوَٰلَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ ٱلْجَنَّةَ

82
00:07:23,808 --> 00:07:26,722
So whenever Umm-Ibrahim(أم إبراهيم) was greeting her son, she told him:

83
00:07:26,766 --> 00:07:31,189
Be careful! And don't allow any of your shortcomings to be seen by Allah.

84
00:07:32,369 --> 00:07:34,484
And then she embraced him and kissed him and said:

85
00:07:35,017 --> 00:07:38,136
May Allah never bring us together except on the Day of Judgment.

86
00:07:39,474 --> 00:07:42,506
This is a woman with Yaqeen(يقين).

87
00:07:43,919 --> 00:07:46,142
She's, making Dua(دُعَا) which is greeting her son,

88
00:07:46,226 --> 00:07:50,162
she's saying: May Allah never bring us together until the day of judgment.

89
00:07:53,121 --> 00:07:56,758
Now Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد), he said:

90
00:07:57,227 --> 00:08:01,079
When we reach the enemy's territory and the people were called to fight.

91
00:08:02,077 --> 00:08:07,520
Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) was in the front and he killed many of the enemy, but then they overwhelmed him and killed him.

92
00:08:09,230 --> 00:08:15,831
On our way back, I told my soldiers not to tell Umm-Ibrahim(أم إبراهيم), that her son was killed until I tell her.

93
00:08:17,053 --> 00:08:20,040
When we entered Al-Basra(ألبصرى), she met me and she said:

94
00:08:20,516 --> 00:08:26,571
Did Allah accept my gift, so that I can celebrate or did Allah rejected so that I should cry,

95
00:08:27,293 --> 00:08:29,588
meaning my gift to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is my son.

96
00:08:30,521 --> 00:08:32,734
Does Allah accept the gift or did he returned back?

97
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:34,903
If He accepted it, I'm going to celebrate.

98
00:08:35,157 --> 00:08:37,740
If Allah is bringing him back to me, I'm going to cry.

99
00:08:38,650 --> 00:08:43,683
The exact opposite of what to be expected from the mother to do.

100
00:08:45,213 --> 00:08:50,761
So Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد) said: Allah did accept your gift and your son died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

101
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:57,184
So she prostrated to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and thanked Allah and said: Thank you Allah for accepting my gift.

102
00:08:59,802 --> 00:09:07,918
The following day, she came to the Mosque and she told Abdul Wahid(عبدالواحد), she told him rejoice, Abshir(أبشر).

103
00:09:08,573 --> 00:09:10,932
So he told her what good news, do you have to give me.?

104
00:09:11,495 --> 00:09:15,515
She said: I saw my son Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) last night in a dream.

105
00:09:16,158 --> 00:09:21,822
He was in a beautiful garden, dressed in green clothes, sitting on a throne made of Pearl,

106
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:28,184
and he had the crown on his head, and he told me: Rejoice, my mother I got married to my bride.

107
00:09:29,823 --> 00:09:35,196
This is an immediate Beshara(بشارة) that the mother received that her son did get married.

108
00:09:40,316 --> 00:09:42,009
The next headline.

109
00:09:44,207 --> 00:09:46,716
The virtue of racing towards Jihad(جهاد).

110
00:09:47,528 --> 00:09:50,631
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says and the fore runners, the fore runners,

111
00:09:51,217 --> 00:09:56,086
those are the ones, who are close to Allah and this is in Al-Waqiah(ألواقعة) Verse 10 & 11.

112
00:09:56,295 --> 00:10:03,237
وَالسَّابِقُونَ السَّابِقُونَ۞ أُولَئِكَ الْمُقَرَّبُونَ۞

113
00:10:04,135 --> 00:10:09,663
There's one view that Sabiqoon(سابقون) are the Sabiqoon(سابقون) of this Ummah(امة).

114
00:10:11,307 --> 00:10:13,728
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and the early generations.

115
00:10:15,107 --> 00:10:16,602
So they have the higher status.

116
00:10:16,682 --> 00:10:22,309
There's another opinion that the Sabiqoon(سابقون) are the ones,

117
00:10:22,349 --> 00:10:26,822
who believe from the other nations before the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ.

118
00:10:28,668 --> 00:10:35,003
But then there's a third opinion and this is narrated by Usman bin Abi Soda(عثمان بن أبي سودة), he said:

119
00:10:35,845 --> 00:10:39,235
We were told that the fore runners mentioned in the verses,

120
00:10:39,637 --> 00:10:43,557
are the first to go out on Jihad(جهاد) and the first to go to Salah(صلاة).

121
00:10:44,469 --> 00:10:49,103
So that the fore runners, or the first in this Ayah(آية) means the first to go to the Masjid(مسجد)

122
00:10:49,745 --> 00:10:52,024
and the first to go out and respond to the call of

123
00:10:52,144 --> 00:10:53,194
حيَّ علی الجهاد

124
00:10:54,235 --> 00:10:59,191
And this narration is in Musnad Ibn Abi Shaibah(مسند إبن أبي شعيبة) and it's authentic Sahih(صحيح).

125
00:10:59,999 --> 00:11:05,130
Now, this Usman bin Abi Soda(عثمان بن أبي سودة), he is among the At-Taba'een(ألتابعين).

126
00:11:05,701 --> 00:11:12,206
And he used to be a Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) and one year, he was asked, Are you going to fight this year?

127
00:11:12,583 --> 00:11:17,150
He said: Yes! I wouldn't want to miss fighting even if I were to make 10,000 dinars.

128
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:22,588
He was one of the At-Taba'een(ألتابعين), who used to go out at least once a year in Ghazoo(غزؤ).

129
00:11:26,643 --> 00:11:29,150
Al-Hasan Ibn Abil Hasan(حسن إبن أبي حسن) said that,

130
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:33,228
Now, in Surah Waqiyah(سورة الواقعة) you have two levels,

131
00:11:33,677 --> 00:11:35,694
you have a Sabiqoon(ألسابقون) and then you have As'haab-Ul-Yameen(أصحاب اليمين).

132
00:11:36,418 --> 00:11:37,665
Now Sabiqoon(ألسابقون) are higher,

133
00:11:38,730 --> 00:11:40,657
Surah Waqiyah(سورة الواقعة) talks about three groups of people

134
00:11:40,707 --> 00:11:43,370
it talks about the Sabiqoon(ألسابقون) first and these are the highest levels in Jannah(جنة),

135
00:11:43,812 --> 00:11:45,306
and the talks about Ahl-Ul-Yameen(أهل اليمين).

136
00:11:46,330 --> 00:11:50,111
And these are the lower levels in Jannah(جنة) and then it talks about us As'hab-Ush- Shimal(ألصحاب الشمال),

137
00:11:50,378 --> 00:11:51,347
the people of hellfire.

138
00:11:51,971 --> 00:11:56,677
So according to the Tafseer(تفسير) of Usman bin Abi Soda(عثمان بن أبي سودة),

139
00:11:58,096 --> 00:12:01,083
the fore runners are the ones, who go out first in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

140
00:12:01,942 --> 00:12:04,809
So he says these are going to be the people in the higher levels of Jannah(جنة).

141
00:12:07,378 --> 00:12:11,151
Al-Hasan Ibn Abil Hasan(حسن إبن أبي حسن) said that the Messenger of Allah sent an army,

142
00:12:11,255 --> 00:12:12,991
and among them was Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذاِبن جبل).

143
00:12:14,986 --> 00:12:17,777
Muadh(معاذ) was late in going out with the army.

144
00:12:18,067 --> 00:12:20,217
So the messenger of Allah saw him and said:

145
00:12:21,176 --> 00:12:24,819
I see that your company is one month ahead of you in paradise.

146
00:12:26,862 --> 00:12:32,227
Now Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذاِبن جبل) did not stay behind because he had some housework to do or business to take care of.

147
00:12:33,504 --> 00:12:35,510
Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذاِبن جبل) said: O Messenger of Allah!

148
00:12:36,674 --> 00:12:40,187
I only stayed behind in order to catch the prayer with you.

149
00:12:40,567 --> 00:12:45,076
And so that you can make Dua(دُعَا) for me, in order for me to be ahead of my company.?

150
00:12:45,762 --> 00:12:48,275
The reason why, I stayed bind is to be ahead of them, not behind them.

151
00:12:49,042 --> 00:12:53,895
I wanted to attend Salah(صلاة) of Jama'a(جماعة) with you, probably could have been Jumuah(جمعة) on that day.

152
00:12:54,908 --> 00:12:59,903
And I wanted you to make a special Dua(دُعَا) for me and exclusive Dua(دُعَا), so that I could be ahead of everybody else,

153
00:13:00,311 --> 00:13:01,528
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him:

154
00:13:02,519 --> 00:13:06,647
No! They are ahead of you! Go and catch up with them!

155
00:13:07,101 --> 00:13:08,455
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

156
00:13:08,884 --> 00:13:13,834
A journey in the morning in the cause of Allah is better than the world and everything on it.

157
00:13:14,188 --> 00:13:19,309
And a journey at the end of the day in the cause of Allah is better than the world and everything on it.

158
00:13:19,469 --> 00:13:22,515
And this is narrated in a Al-Sunan Al-Bayhaqi(سنن ألبيهقي),

159
00:13:23,114 --> 00:13:23,994
so go out when?

160
00:13:24,838 --> 00:13:27,205
Hadith(حديث) says in the morning and in the evening.

161
00:13:27,617 --> 00:13:29,449
Now An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي), he comments and he says

162
00:13:29,489 --> 00:13:33,097
the Hadith(حديث) does not restrict rewards to the beginning or the end of the day,

163
00:13:33,721 --> 00:13:39,742
it is just to point out that spending a very little time in the cause of Allah carries a very great reward.

164
00:13:40,873 --> 00:13:44,452
So whenever you go out there it is worth, a world and everything in it.

165
00:13:45,441 --> 00:13:48,291
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:

166
00:13:49,286 --> 00:13:53,673
Whoever goes out in His cause was no objective, but fighting in His sake,

167
00:13:54,184 --> 00:14:00,270
and believing in Him and His messengers, Allah will guarantee for him, either to enter him into paradise,

168
00:14:00,790 --> 00:14:03,753
or to return him home with rewards or booty.

169
00:14:04,701 --> 00:14:10,407
In the name of whom Muhammad(محمد) soul is in His hand, whoever is injured in the path of Allah,

170
00:14:10,858 --> 00:14:14,934
the injury would come on the Day of Judgment, as it was in this world.

171
00:14:15,562 --> 00:14:19,411
The color is that of blood, and the smell is that of musk.

172
00:14:20,107 --> 00:14:22,869
In the name of whom Muhammad(محمد) Soul is in His hand.

173
00:14:23,371 --> 00:14:26,173
If it wasn't for making things difficult on Muslims,

174
00:14:26,577 --> 00:14:29,736
I wouldn't have stayed behind any army leaving in the path of Allah.

175
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:33,483
But I'm unable to find sustenance for the Muslims, who stay behind.

176
00:14:34,207 --> 00:14:37,572
So these are Muslims who weren't trying to find an excuse to stay behind.

177
00:14:37,883 --> 00:14:43,748
These were Muslims who dearly wanted to go out but they couldn't, because they had no support.

178
00:14:45,025 --> 00:14:49,208
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ is staying behind in Jihad(جهاد) that is Fardh Kafaya(فرض كِفاية), not Farz Ain(فرض عين)

179
00:14:50,789 --> 00:14:52,469
this is Fardh Kafaya(فرض كِفاية), it is Ghazoo(غزؤ).

180
00:14:52,818 --> 00:14:58,078
And we understand how difficult it was because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says about them,

181
00:14:58,582 --> 00:15:03,382
تَوَلَّواْ وَّأَعْيُنُهُمْ تَفِيضُ مِنَ ٱلدَّمْعِ حَزَنًا أَلَّا يَجِدُواْ مَا يُنفِقُونَ۝

182
00:15:04,038 --> 00:15:06,775
That they're turning away with tears in their eyes

183
00:15:06,884 --> 00:15:10,132
because they have no money to go out in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

184
00:15:10,856 --> 00:15:14,636
they would go to a Rasool Ullah and they would say, Jahizna(جحزنا), finances us!

185
00:15:14,716 --> 00:15:20,510
Rasool Allah ﷺ would say: I have nothing to give you, they would walked away with tears rolling down their cheeks.

186
00:15:21,380 --> 00:15:24,907
There's so sorry that they're unable to fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

187
00:15:26,198 --> 00:15:29,443
So you can see the contrast between the Mumineen(مومنين) and Munafiqeen(مُنافقين).

188
00:15:29,535 --> 00:15:33,314
The Munafiqeen(مُنافقين) they come to Rasool Allah ﷺ, inventing every type of excuse

189
00:15:34,167 --> 00:15:40,052
and when Rasool Allah ﷺ excuses them, they go away happy feeling that they have achieved something.

190
00:15:41,051 --> 00:15:46,208
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says, In the name of whom Muhammad(محمد) soul is in His hand.

191
00:15:46,931 --> 00:15:50,938
I wish, I could fight in the Cause of Allah, and then be killed,

192
00:15:51,328 --> 00:15:55,073
and then fight, and then be killed, and then fight, and then be killed,

193
00:15:56,871 --> 00:15:57,942
and this is in Sahih Muslim(صحيح المسلم).

194
00:15:58,127 --> 00:16:02,231
Now An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي), it's either An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي) or Ibn Hajar(إبن حجَر).

195
00:16:02,405 --> 00:16:08,575
It poses the question, how could Rasool Allah ﷺ desire to die, when he's guaranteed that he's not going to die,

196
00:16:09,192 --> 00:16:16,523
for him is Mustahih(مستحيح), dying of Rasool Allah ﷺ in the battlefield is something that is impossible,

197
00:16:17,244 --> 00:16:18,322
because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said:

198
00:16:18,381 --> 00:16:19,820
وَاللَّهُ يَعْصِمُكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ

199
00:16:20,292 --> 00:16:22,451
Allah is going to protect you, from people.

200
00:16:23,741 --> 00:16:24,918
An-Nawwawi(ألنووِي) says that

201
00:16:25,387 --> 00:16:31,279
this first of all shows that it's allowed to ask for something, even though you know that cannot happen to you.

202
00:16:31,636 --> 00:16:37,634
And it's to show that Rasool Allah ﷺ was so keen about the issue of Shahadah(شَهَادَة)

203
00:16:37,659 --> 00:16:40,754
that he even desired it for himself being the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

204
00:16:41,077 --> 00:16:45,079
In other words, the reason why he said it, is an encouragement to Ummah(امة) to follow this path.

205
00:16:45,159 --> 00:16:51,502
But even I, who will not be able to get it because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has guaranteed me safety in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) from the hands of men,

206
00:16:51,756 --> 00:16:57,548
even I would have desired that I would die in the sake of Allah and then come again and then die and come again, and then die.

207
00:16:58,262 --> 00:17:05,141
Abdullah Bin Mukhaireez(عبدالله بن محيريز) narrates that his father was sent into the army, in the army of summer.

208
00:17:05,808 --> 00:17:07,867
So they had to an army of summer, and an army of winter.

209
00:17:08,927 --> 00:17:10,567
So he became extremely ill.

210
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:13,165
He said: Oh, my son!

211
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:16,096
Carry me into the land of the Romans.

212
00:17:17,164 --> 00:17:21,903
The battlefield, wasn't the land of the Romans, he became ill he told his son carry me further,

213
00:17:22,980 --> 00:17:28,126
so I carried him, And he was still traveling through the land when he said: My son go fast.

214
00:17:29,693 --> 00:17:31,005
I said: Father, but you're ill.

215
00:17:31,818 --> 00:17:36,913
He said: My son, I want my death to meet me in the land of the Romans.

216
00:17:38,068 --> 00:17:40,597
So I continued carrying him, until he died.

217
00:17:42,672 --> 00:17:47,146
The son said: I was worried how would I find anybody to pray Janazah(جنازة) on him

218
00:17:47,252 --> 00:17:49,248
because he died a natural death, it wasn't a Shahadah(شَهَادَة).

219
00:17:49,957 --> 00:17:54,167
So he was wondering where is he gonna find anybody to pray on him, in Hims(حمص) in Syria,

220
00:17:54,584 --> 00:17:58,636
when there are no Muslims around this is in the depths of the land of the Romans,

221
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:00,300
so the son said:

222
00:18:01,285 --> 00:18:08,171
I then saw ranks of men, whom I'm never saw before, dressed in white, praying on my father.

223
00:18:10,134 --> 00:18:15,744
These are must have been angels whose Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ sent to pray Janazah(جنازة).

224
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:19,916
Now this is an interesting story narrated by Ibn Asakir(إبن عساكر).

225
00:18:20,599 --> 00:18:22,567
The one before also was by Ibn Asakir(إبن عساكر).

226
00:18:23,530 --> 00:18:25,752
This is the story of Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبو مسلم ألخولاني),

227
00:18:25,832 --> 00:18:29,911
we talked about Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبو مسلم ألخولاني) before, do you remember, what we said about him.?

228
00:18:32,426 --> 00:18:35,402
Let's see if, your memories are fresh.

229
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:40,698
What did we say about Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبو مسلم ألخولاني)? I talked about it, I think in the previous session.

230
00:18:42,056 --> 00:18:48,989
A Karamah(كرامة) happened to him. Which Karamah(كرامة) was that? Which one? The fire! the fire! the fire!

231
00:18:49,974 --> 00:18:51,452
He was the one who wasn't burnt in the fire.

232
00:18:52,681 --> 00:18:55,678
Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبو مسلم ألخولاني), he then set out in Jihad(جهاد) Fee Ardh-Ir-Ar-Rome(في أرض ألروم).

233
00:18:56,385 --> 00:19:03,237
Saad Ibn Abdul Aziz(سعد إبن عبدالعزيز) said: Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبو مسلم ألخولاني) died in the territory of the Romans.

234
00:19:03,663 --> 00:19:06,417
During the reign of Muawiah Bin Abi Sufiyan رضي الله عنه.

235
00:19:07,349 --> 00:19:08,627
He told Bisr Bin Arta'a(بسربن أبي أرطأء),

236
00:19:08,667 --> 00:19:13,739
Bisr Bin Arta'a(بسربن أبي أرطأء) was the leader of the army and Bisr Bin Arta'a he has some heroic stories.

237
00:19:14,672 --> 00:19:21,239
And I think that Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس), will talk about them in, in his chapter about the history of Jihad(جهاد).

238
00:19:21,663 --> 00:19:26,414
Bisr Bin Arta'a(بسربن أبي أرطأء), was the head of the army.

239
00:19:26,758 --> 00:19:28,695
So Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبو مسلم ألخولاني) went to him and he said:

240
00:19:30,104 --> 00:19:35,820
Appoint me, Now Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبو مسلم ألخولاني) was already injured that he was on the verge of dying.

241
00:19:36,257 --> 00:19:37,275
So he's dying as a Shaheed(شَهِيد).

242
00:19:38,472 --> 00:19:40,556
So he goes to Bisr Bin Arta'a(بسربن أبي أرطأء) and he says:

243
00:19:41,709 --> 00:19:46,396
I want you to appoint me as an Ameer(أمير) over the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء), who died.

244
00:19:47,741 --> 00:19:51,077
He wants him, to appoint him as an Ameer(أمير) over the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء).

245
00:19:52,578 --> 00:19:54,920
And I want you to give me a banner of war.

246
00:19:56,309 --> 00:20:01,673
And I want you to make my grave, the closest of all the graves of the martyrs to the enemy.

247
00:20:02,738 --> 00:20:03,894
So he is asking for three things.

248
00:20:03,967 --> 00:20:08,494
Number one, you appoint me as an Ameer(أمير) over the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء), the ones who died.

249
00:20:09,605 --> 00:20:12,223
Number two, you give me the banner of war, Ar-Raya(ألراية).

250
00:20:13,133 --> 00:20:18,846
And number three, I want my grave to be the furthest into the land of the enemy, deep, in the territory of the enemy.

251
00:20:19,362 --> 00:20:20,287
Why? He said:

252
00:20:20,849 --> 00:20:22,230
Because on the Day of Judgment,

253
00:20:22,966 --> 00:20:28,294
I want to be resurrected carrying my banner and leading the martyrs on Youm-Ul-Qayamah(يوم القيامة).

254
00:20:30,144 --> 00:20:32,832
So he wants to carry on, even, on the day of judgment.

255
00:20:32,912 --> 00:20:38,131
He wants to come on the Day of Judgment carrying that banner of war, with all of the Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) behind him.

256
00:20:40,065 --> 00:20:42,309
The virtues of the dust in the path of Allah.

257
00:20:43,105 --> 00:20:44,464
The messenger of Allah said:

258
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:51,983
Whoever has his feet dirty in the path of Allah, Allah will save him from hellfire.

259
00:20:52,516 --> 00:20:53,489
And that's in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

260
00:20:54,222 --> 00:20:55,895
And this goes back to what we were talking about.

261
00:20:57,337 --> 00:21:00,089
You know, with other Ibadaat(عبادات) that the whole that has given a Fazeelah(فضيلة).

262
00:21:01,415 --> 00:21:08,153
But with Jihad(جهاد) it's broken into bits and pieces and every bit and piece, carries such a big Ajr(أجْر) with it.

263
00:21:08,645 --> 00:21:16,241
So here the dust, even the dust in Sabeel-Lillah(سَبيل الله) carries an Ajr(أجْر).

264
00:21:18,913 --> 00:21:22,788
In Musnad Imam Ahmad(مُسنداِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ), Abu Darda(أبودرداء) narrated, the Messenger of Allah said:

265
00:21:23,258 --> 00:21:28,834
Allah will not combine in the lungs of His servant, the dust of the path of Allah with the smoke of hellfire

266
00:21:29,766 --> 00:21:32,072
and whoever gets his feet dirty in the path of Allah,

267
00:21:32,456 --> 00:21:37,077
Allah will keep him away from hellfire the distance of 1000 years travel for a fast horse.

268
00:21:38,890 --> 00:21:42,632
And whoever is injured in the path of Allah will receive the seal of martyrdom.

269
00:21:43,386 --> 00:21:47,798
The injury comes on the Day of Judgment with the color of saffron and the smell of musk.

270
00:21:48,459 --> 00:21:52,983
It is a sign that would be recognized by all the creation, the beginning and the end,

271
00:21:53,406 --> 00:21:56,226
they will say, he has the stamp of martyrs.

272
00:21:56,953 --> 00:22:04,203
When you do something for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, Allah takes, takes care of all of the other needs that you might have.

273
00:22:06,574 --> 00:22:12,495
As a human being, we have a natural instinct of wanting to show off,

274
00:22:14,106 --> 00:22:17,787
of wanting to be famous, wanting to be recognized.

275
00:22:17,941 --> 00:22:22,594
I mean these are, these are traits in the human being, that we are created with.

276
00:22:23,486 --> 00:22:27,924
Now Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tells you to put all of that aside and do the deed, purely for Him.

277
00:22:28,962 --> 00:22:35,376
So you're not showing off, you're not doing it to be recognized, you're not doing it to be praised.

278
00:22:35,914 --> 00:22:37,484
You're doing it purely for the sake of Allah.

279
00:22:38,313 --> 00:22:42,496
Because you did it purely for the sake of Allah, Allah will take care of all of the other needs.

280
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:49,566
So, this martyr who was doing it purely for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

281
00:22:50,231 --> 00:22:55,694
on the Day of Judgment Allah will give him that badge of honor that is seen by all of the creation, not just the people of his time.

282
00:22:57,501 --> 00:22:59,255
Because the Shaheed(شَهِيد), who was doing it for Riya(رِيَاء),

283
00:22:59,743 --> 00:23:04,721
and went to hellfire because of it, only got recognized by the soldiers that he knew.

284
00:23:05,479 --> 00:23:07,554
Maybe it's not more than 10, 20, 30 people.

285
00:23:08,580 --> 00:23:10,144
And he ends up going to hellfire because of it.

286
00:23:11,998 --> 00:23:16,327
While the person who is doing it for the sake of Allah will end up having the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) witness that,

287
00:23:16,717 --> 00:23:20,733
and the other Shuhadaa(شُهَدآء) and the Saliheen(صالحين) and the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

288
00:23:21,467 --> 00:23:25,977
all of the creation will be brought together on the day of judgment to witness that this man is the Shaheed(شَهِيد)

289
00:23:26,057 --> 00:23:29,157
and the Shaheed(شَهِيد) will carry that badge of honor with him wherever he goes.

290
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:34,726
But he do something for the sake of Allah, Allah will, will give you more than what you could have got,

291
00:23:35,764 --> 00:23:39,260
If you did something for somebody else, for another object able reason.

292
00:23:42,299 --> 00:23:48,467
And whoever fights in the path of Allah for a period equivalent to the time it takes to milk a camel is guaranteed paradise.

293
00:23:50,915 --> 00:23:53,115
The virtues of riding the sea in Jihad(جهاد):

294
00:23:58,463 --> 00:24:00,036
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك) narrated,

295
00:24:01,539 --> 00:24:07,353
the Messenger of Allah, would visit Umm Haram Bint Malhaan(أم حرام بنت ملحان), she would feed him.

296
00:24:07,836 --> 00:24:10,375
Umm Haram(أم حرام) was the wife of Ubada Bin Samit(عبادة بن صامت).

297
00:24:12,302 --> 00:24:17,989
One day when he visited her after she fed him, she sat down to comb his hair.

298
00:24:19,057 --> 00:24:20,613
The Messenger of Allah fell asleep.

299
00:24:21,505 --> 00:24:22,631
He then woke up laughing.

300
00:24:23,892 --> 00:24:27,831
She asked him what is making you laugh.

301
00:24:28,954 --> 00:24:30,114
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

302
00:24:30,626 --> 00:24:39,397
I was presented with some of my nation, who were going out to fight in the cause of Allah, riding the sea, like kings on thrones.

303
00:24:40,587 --> 00:24:43,333
Now when the Arabs of Makkah and Madina.

304
00:24:44,413 --> 00:24:50,855
They were do traveling by land, and only a few of them would travel by sea

305
00:24:50,935 --> 00:24:54,682
and it wasn't something that was in the custom of the Arabs of Hijaz(حجاز),

306
00:24:55,340 --> 00:24:59,775
some of them like Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) for example, we know that they did travel by sea,

307
00:25:00,245 --> 00:25:02,807
the Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) of Al-Habsha(ألحبشه) also traveled by sea,

308
00:25:03,201 --> 00:25:11,071
but their business travel was done by land, they would go to Yemen and then that they would go to Syria, so it was on land.

309
00:25:12,624 --> 00:25:16,634
And the Arabs didn't fight in the sea.

310
00:25:17,885 --> 00:25:22,087
If they did travel in the sea, it was for business reasons but they did not fight in the sea.

311
00:25:23,731 --> 00:25:28,471
It was only after Islam, that they started fighting in the sea

312
00:25:28,511 --> 00:25:34,697
and the one, who was is considered to be the founder of the Islamic Navy is Muavia Bin Abi Sufiyan(معاوية بن أبي سفيان).

313
00:25:35,340 --> 00:25:36,590
When he was the Ameer(أمير) of Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

314
00:25:37,838 --> 00:25:42,792
Not when it was Khalifah(خليفه), when he was Ameer(أمير) in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

315
00:25:43,108 --> 00:25:45,750
That's when he sought permission to fight in the sea,

316
00:25:45,830 --> 00:25:48,324
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was reluctant to agree.

317
00:25:48,754 --> 00:25:54,060
I mean, that shows you how cautious they were when it came to this area because it was an unknown area to them.

318
00:25:55,296 --> 00:26:02,015
So Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that in his dream, he saw the first Muslims, who will go out in the sea,

319
00:26:02,203 --> 00:26:05,972
and he said I saw them riding the sea, like kings on thrones.

320
00:26:07,957 --> 00:26:10,722
When Umm Haram(أم حرام), she heard that and what was her response?

321
00:26:11,301 --> 00:26:12,704
She said: Am I going to be one of them.?

322
00:26:13,316 --> 00:26:15,340
That's the first thing that came on mind.

323
00:26:15,833 --> 00:26:16,587
Now this is a woman.

324
00:26:17,988 --> 00:26:18,339
Right!

325
00:26:19,126 --> 00:26:23,724
But Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) they were so attached to this and whenever there was Khair(خير) they wanted to be part of it,

326
00:26:23,792 --> 00:26:26,297
she said, will I be part of it?

327
00:26:26,377 --> 00:26:30,176
She said: O Messenger of Allah! Ask Allah that I be one of them,

328
00:26:30,818 --> 00:26:33,120
you know like in the Hadith(حديث) of the Dajjal(دجال).

329
00:26:34,067 --> 00:26:37,986
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said that Ad-Dajjal(ألدجال) will spent 40 days among you,

330
00:26:38,469 --> 00:26:44,344
one day is like a year and then one day is like a month and then the next day is like a week and then they're going to be regular days.

331
00:26:44,585 --> 00:26:45,651
What did the Sahabah(صحابه) say?

332
00:26:45,963 --> 00:26:50,054
I mean you could bring up tons of hypothetical questions.

333
00:26:50,491 --> 00:26:52,867
What happened, did the rotation of the earth change?

334
00:26:53,344 --> 00:27:00,143
Or they could have asked, is there going to be a night, and for how long will might be on that day that is a year long.

335
00:27:00,543 --> 00:27:05,453
You know you could come up with tons of questions, and your questions are a reflection of the way you think.

336
00:27:05,533 --> 00:27:08,150
The only question that the Sahabah(صحابه) had on mind is?

337
00:27:08,408 --> 00:27:11,840
O Rasool Ullah, how will we pray on that day, that's like a year.?

338
00:27:13,105 --> 00:27:14,852
So, it shows you how they were thinking.

339
00:27:16,037 --> 00:27:20,381
هل أَتَكْفِينَا فيه صَلَاةُ يَومٍ؟ قالَ رسول الله صلى عليه وسلم : لَا، اقْدُرُوا له قَدْرَهُ،

340
00:27:20,771 --> 00:27:24,427
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No! You have to give it a proper estimate.

341
00:27:26,452 --> 00:27:31,917
So Umm Haram(أم حرام) here is saying: Immediately O Rasool Ullah ask Allah to make me among them.

342
00:27:33,065 --> 00:27:35,935
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: He prayed for her.

343
00:27:36,250 --> 00:27:40,690
so Rasool Allah ﷺ  prayed for her, and in another Hadith(حديث) he said: You will be among them.

344
00:27:41,237 --> 00:27:42,454
And then he went to sleep again.

345
00:27:43,248 --> 00:27:46,673
So he woke up another time laughing, she said: What is making you laugh?

346
00:27:47,038 --> 00:27:51,713
He said: I saw another group and described them as he did before, she said:

347
00:27:52,093 --> 00:27:54,300
Pray to Allah that I am one of them,

348
00:27:54,986 --> 00:27:56,822
again she wants to be part of the second group.

349
00:27:57,245 --> 00:27:59,663
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You are with the first group.

350
00:28:00,379 --> 00:28:01,901
You are with the first group, that's it.

351
00:28:02,877 --> 00:28:05,318
Don't worry you get the share of it, but you are in the first group.

352
00:28:06,726 --> 00:28:10,266
Even though this seems to be a lone opinion

353
00:28:10,386 --> 00:28:15,338
but Ibn Hazam(إبن حزم) considers that the second group that Rasool Allah ﷺ saw,

354
00:28:16,017 --> 00:28:18,491
were the Muslims who opened the Andlus(ألأندلس).

355
00:28:19,576 --> 00:28:24,254
But it's the opinion of Ibn Hazam(إبن حزم) that there is a special fazal(فضل), for the ones who open the Andlus(ألأندلس),

356
00:28:24,731 --> 00:28:28,778
because he considers them to be part of this Hadith(حديث) in Sahih Muslim( صحيح مسلم),

357
00:28:29,191 --> 00:28:30,470
he considers them to be the second.

358
00:28:30,741 --> 00:28:33,305
Umm Haram(أم حرام) heard the Messenger of Allah say,

359
00:28:33,783 --> 00:28:37,910
the first of my Ummah(امة) to ride the sea in the cause of Allah are forgiven.

360
00:28:40,080 --> 00:28:44,364
Umm Haram(أم حرام) said, O Messenger of Allah, am I among them?

361
00:28:44,475 --> 00:28:50,722
He said: Yes you are! He then said the first of my Ummah(امة) to attack the city of Caesar, are forgiven,

362
00:28:50,896 --> 00:28:52,707
she said: Am I among them? He said: No!

363
00:28:53,578 --> 00:28:54,971
This Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

364
00:28:55,710 --> 00:29:01,237
This Hadith(حديث) also is an indication of the special honor of naval warfare and also the special honor of fighting the Romans,

365
00:29:01,380 --> 00:29:02,787
because it says that they are forgiven.

366
00:29:06,341 --> 00:29:08,854
Ka'ab Al Ahbar(كعب ألأحبار), he said:

367
00:29:09,362 --> 00:29:12,357
When a man first sets his foot on the ship.

368
00:29:13,706 --> 00:29:15,754
He leaves all of his sins behind him,

369
00:29:16,606 --> 00:29:18,900
and becomes clean like the day he was born,

370
00:29:19,276 --> 00:29:25,372
and the one, who suffers seasickness, is like the injured, who is pouring his blood in the path of Allah.

371
00:29:25,435 --> 00:29:27,977
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) look at, you know,

372
00:29:28,057 --> 00:29:29,865
ألجزاء من جنس العمل

373
00:29:30,151 --> 00:29:33,516
 The payback is according to the deeds.

374
00:29:35,085 --> 00:29:38,799
Seasickness for any of you, who has experienced it.

375
00:29:39,095 --> 00:29:46,898
First of all there's, dizziness, and then the stomach, the whole digestive system goes into a crash.

376
00:29:48,693 --> 00:29:54,510
The stomach is squeezing out whatever is in there and when there's nothing left, it's still squeezing out

377
00:29:55,059 --> 00:29:56,145
trying to get something out.

378
00:29:56,891 --> 00:30:00,344
So you find the person who has seasickness is trying to vomit and nothing is coming out

379
00:30:00,424 --> 00:30:02,924
and they would end up trying to drink anything

380
00:30:03,796 --> 00:30:08,830
in order to vomit it because the pain of trying to vomit and nothing is coming out is so aggravating.

381
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:13,073
And this carries on and on and on for hours.

382
00:30:14,009 --> 00:30:19,622
I mean somebody, they say about 20% of the population are susceptible to seasickness,

383
00:30:19,887 --> 00:30:26,379
and it's just continuous agony as long as the waves are rocking that boat that secrecy sea sickness carries on.

384
00:30:28,490 --> 00:30:33,546
So Rasool Allah ﷺ says: It's like somebody who's pouring blood, because they're continuously trying to vomit.

385
00:30:33,987 --> 00:30:39,243
So Rasool Allah ﷺ saying it's like somebody who's continuously pouring blood as Al-Jarih Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(ألجريح فِي سَبيل الله).

386
00:30:40,275 --> 00:30:45,216
This is in Saeed Ibn Mansoor(سعيد إبن منصور) in Sunan(سُنَن) and it is Hasan(حسن).

387
00:30:46,587 --> 00:30:51,537
And the one, who is patient in the sea is like a king with a crown on his head.

388
00:30:52,639 --> 00:30:56,263
Hayyan Afri(حَيًّ آفري), he is one of a Tabieen(تابعين) in Egypt.

389
00:30:57,336 --> 00:31:02,312
He said: We were sitting with Abdullah Ibn Amr Bin Al-Aas(عبدالله بن عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) under the Alexandria lighthouse,

390
00:31:02,683 --> 00:31:05,675
the lighthouse, apparently, at that time still existed.

391
00:31:07,682 --> 00:31:10,332
It doesn't exist now anymore but at the time it was there.

392
00:31:10,784 --> 00:31:14,071
I think it was broken down in earth quake.

393
00:31:15,537 --> 00:31:17,551
And it used to be one of the seven wonders of the world.

394
00:31:19,763 --> 00:31:23,970
So, he says we were sitting with Abdullah Ibn Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو) under the Alexandra Lighthouse

395
00:31:24,010 --> 00:31:26,347
when the ships of Jihad(جهاد) were embarking on their journey.

396
00:31:26,743 --> 00:31:34,177
So Abdullah Ibn Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو) and some of Tabieen(تابعين), were watching the Muslims go out in the sea.

397
00:31:34,752 --> 00:31:39,125
Abdullah(عبدالله) asked, ask them he said: Where are their sins?

398
00:31:40,360 --> 00:31:43,253
To these Muslim sailors, where are their sins?

399
00:31:45,485 --> 00:31:47,573
So we said: They're hanging to their necks.

400
00:31:48,993 --> 00:31:50,641
You're carrying your sins with you.

401
00:31:51,207 --> 00:31:52,042
Your sins on you.

402
00:31:53,251 --> 00:31:54,392
Abdullah Ibn Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو) said:

403
00:31:55,013 --> 00:31:55,647
No! They're not.

404
00:31:55,866 --> 00:32:00,101
In the Name of Allah, they have left all of their sins on these beaches,

405
00:32:00,381 --> 00:32:04,209
and now they're walking free of sin, with the exception of their debts.

406
00:32:06,114 --> 00:32:08,017
And Abdullah Ibn Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو), he also says,

407
00:32:08,662 --> 00:32:11,738
and this is Musnad Ibn Abi Shaibah(مسند إبن أبي شعيبة).

408
00:32:12,402 --> 00:32:15,531
He says, Allah laughs at the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) of the sea, many times.

409
00:32:16,483 --> 00:32:20,473
He laughs at them when they first ride the ship leaving their families and wealth behind.

410
00:32:20,810 --> 00:32:23,615
He laughs at them when the ship starts to walk in sea,

411
00:32:24,533 --> 00:32:27,519
and he laughs at them when they first see the shore.

412
00:32:28,620 --> 00:32:31,092
Now just imagine if Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is laughing at you.

413
00:32:31,838 --> 00:32:33,844
When Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ laughs at them three times.

414
00:32:34,702 --> 00:32:39,360
Now, in addition to that, you know satisfaction that you would have in your heart and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is watching you

415
00:32:39,440 --> 00:32:42,270
and laughing at you and Rasool Allah ﷺ says in another Hadith(حديث)

416
00:32:42,776 --> 00:32:47,316
that if Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ laughs at somebody, Allah will never enter that person in hellfire.

417
00:32:48,249 --> 00:32:53,720
If Allah smiles at you, He granted Itq Minan-Naar(عتق من النار), he will be saved from hellfire.

418
00:32:55,587 --> 00:33:00,143
Now the author of Al-Mughni(ألمغني) and others from the school of Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) state

419
00:33:00,183 --> 00:33:07,275
that the expeditions of the sea are greater reward than those of land, since it is more difficult and dangerous.

420
00:33:07,796 --> 00:33:09,629
In my opinion, Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) is saying:

421
00:33:10,075 --> 00:33:14,823
There should be no difference of opinion and that due to the aforementioned Hadith(حديث)

422
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:17,725
that state the great status of Jihad(جهاد) in the sea.

423
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:24,945
It should be stated, however, that one should not ride the sea, when it is so dangerous that the likelihood of survival is very slim.

424
00:33:25,377 --> 00:33:32,626
The next section was a bit long in the book of Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) but I Just chose an Ayah(آية) and the Hadith(حديث),

425
00:33:33,134 --> 00:33:35,699
 and this is chapter on the virtues of horses,

426
00:33:36,125 --> 00:33:37,961
and keeping them for the purpose of Jihad(جهاد).

427
00:33:40,319 --> 00:33:41,371
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

428
00:33:41,554 --> 00:33:54,924
وَأَعِدّوا لَهُم مَا استَطَعتُم مِن قُوَّةٍ وَمِن رِباطِ الخَيلِ تُرهِبونَ بِهِ عَدُوَّ اللَّهِ وَعَدُوَّكُم

429
00:33:55,586 --> 00:34:04,127
وَعَدُوَّكُم وَآخَرينَ مِن دونِهِم لا تَعلَمونَهُمُ اللَّهُ يَعلَمُهُم ۚ

430
00:34:04,515 --> 00:34:15,905
وَما تُنفِقوا مِن شَيءٍ في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ يُوَفَّ إِلَيكُم وَأَنتُم لا تُظلَمونَ۞

431
00:34:16,218 --> 00:34:21,149
And prepare against them whatever you are able of power and of steeds of war,

432
00:34:21,574 --> 00:34:27,063
by which you may terrify the enemy of Allah and your enemy and others besides them,

433
00:34:27,463 --> 00:34:29,905
 whom you do not know but Allah knows.

434
00:34:30,237 --> 00:34:37,205
And whoever and whatever you spend in the Cause of Allah will be fully repaid to you, and you will not be wronged.

435
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:43,277
وَأَعِدّوا لَهُم مَا استَطَعتُم مِن قُوَّةٍ وَمِن رِباطِ الخَيلِ تُرهِبونَ بِهِ عَدُوَّ اللَّهِ وَعَدُوَّكُم

436
00:34:44,577 --> 00:34:48,238
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated the messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

437
00:34:48,484 --> 00:34:53,115
Whoever keeps a horse for the sake of Allah, believing in Allah, and His promise,

438
00:34:53,195 --> 00:35:00,685
then his horses feeding, drinking, droppings and urine are going to be on a scale of good deeds on the day of judgment.

439
00:35:01,946 --> 00:35:06,071
 All of this will be lumped and put on your scale of good deeds on the day of judgment.

440
00:35:08,024 --> 00:35:10,376
We move on to the next section.

441
00:35:11,100 --> 00:35:13,735
The virtue of fear in the path of Allah.

442
00:35:15,567 --> 00:35:20,637
Now, as a human being, you have these feelings and they are natural,

443
00:35:20,964 --> 00:35:26,079
I mean Islam is does not expect you to be an angel, and you change your human makeup,

444
00:35:26,447 --> 00:35:28,314
as a human being, you will have fear.

445
00:35:29,374 --> 00:35:33,583
When it comes to fear, even Musa عليه السّلام is experienced it.

446
00:35:34,809 --> 00:35:37,782
And Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ tell us about his first encounter with Wahi(وحي).

447
00:35:38,793 --> 00:35:48,119
When Musa(موسى) was in the wilderness and spoke to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and his stab turned into a snake.

448
00:35:48,366 --> 00:35:49,264
What did Musa(موسى) do?

449
00:35:50,908 --> 00:35:53,060
وَلَّى مُدْبِرًا وَلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ

450
00:35:53,596 --> 00:35:56,183
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ said: He fled and didn't even look back.

451
00:35:57,294 --> 00:35:57,760
وَلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ

452
00:35:57,815 --> 00:35:59,780
He didn't even turn behind to see.

453
00:36:00,275 --> 00:36:03,043
So it wasn't just fear, he ran away.

454
00:36:03,668 --> 00:36:06,721
He just ran away when he saw stab turning into a serpent.

455
00:36:08,695 --> 00:36:15,056
But the thing is that the Tarbiya Al-Eemaniyyah(تربيعة ألإيمانية), the Eeman(ايمان), training that you go through

456
00:36:16,659 --> 00:36:23,638
channels those fears feelings, it doesn't stop them, it doesn't wipe them out, it's just channels them in the right direction.

457
00:36:24,943 --> 00:36:31,024
So the fear that you have remains there, it doesn't really go anywhere it's there but it's channeled in the right direction.

458
00:36:31,580 --> 00:36:32,635
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

459
00:36:32,685 --> 00:36:34,765
أتَخْشَوْنَهُمْ ۚ فَاللَّهُ أَحَقُّ أَن تَخْشَوْهُ

460
00:36:35,638 --> 00:36:39,650
You fear the enemy, you should be fearing Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

461
00:36:42,693 --> 00:36:46,150
So that fear still remains in your heart but goes to the right place,

462
00:36:46,398 --> 00:36:48,959
you end up fearing Allah rather than fearing the enemy.

463
00:36:51,270 --> 00:36:52,815
And you would notice that Islam,

464
00:36:53,138 --> 00:36:57,831
the Tarbiyyah(تربيعة) of Qur'an, seals, all of the gaps,

465
00:36:58,725 --> 00:37:01,311
in which Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) can come to you in Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

466
00:37:01,749 --> 00:37:05,857
All of them are sealed, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ takes care of every single need.

467
00:37:08,425 --> 00:37:13,600
If it is the issue of pain, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

468
00:37:14,314 --> 00:37:19,990
إِن تَكُونُواْ تَأْلَمُونَ فَإِنَّهُمْ يَأْلَمُونَ كَمَا تَأْلَمُونَ ۖ وَتَرْجُونَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَا يَرْجُونَ ۗ

469
00:37:20,851 --> 00:37:21,793
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

470
00:37:22,090 --> 00:37:28,284
If you feel pain. Well, they also feel pain, but you are expecting a reward from Allah that they're not expecting.

471
00:37:29,242 --> 00:37:33,831
So Allah is telling you that they are also feeling pain, but you are expecting something that they don't expect.

472
00:37:34,996 --> 00:37:36,341
So everything is taken care of.

473
00:37:36,410 --> 00:37:44,001
So, that's spiritually, you will be mobilized to the limit and Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) cannot come to you from any direction.

474
00:37:45,246 --> 00:37:46,581
The Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) can't feel fear.

475
00:37:48,046 --> 00:37:55,932
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in this Hadith(حديث) which is narrated by Ibn Mubarak(إبن المبارك) and Ibn Shayba(إبن شعيبة) and At-Tabrani(ألطبراني),

476
00:37:56,720 --> 00:37:58,526
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) says:

477
00:37:58,893 --> 00:38:04,662
If the heart of the believer trembles in the path of Allah, that would shake down his sins,

478
00:38:04,910 --> 00:38:07,434
just like the shaking of a cluster of figs.

479
00:38:09,275 --> 00:38:10,993
Being in the battle is not an easy experience

480
00:38:11,073 --> 00:38:19,569
and that's why when Rasool Allah ﷺ was asked how come the Shaheed(شَهِيد) doesn't go through the faza(فزع) of the Day of Judgment,

481
00:38:19,650 --> 00:38:20,700
the fear on the day of judgment.?

482
00:38:20,740 --> 00:38:21,833
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say?

483
00:38:22,200 --> 00:38:24,912
كفَى ببارقةِ السُّيوفِ علَى رأسِهِ فتنةً

484
00:38:25,467 --> 00:38:29,360
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It's enough that swords were shining on top of his head.

485
00:38:30,020 --> 00:38:34,396
You know that glimmering of light when light reflects off a sharp sword,

486
00:38:34,763 --> 00:38:38,000
and you see that coming in your eye and the sword is right on top of your head.

487
00:38:38,229 --> 00:38:42,627
That's the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) in itself. So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: That's sufficient of a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for that person.

488
00:38:43,525 --> 00:38:48,134
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that when that heart shakes and trembles,

489
00:38:48,542 --> 00:38:54,006
that shaking makes all of the sins dropped down like leaves of a tree,

490
00:38:55,469 --> 00:38:59,002
and Abdullah bin Amr Bin Al-Aas(عبدالله بن عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:

491
00:38:59,644 --> 00:39:04,522
Any expedition that fights in the path of Allah, and win or come back safe,

492
00:39:04,934 --> 00:39:07,987
have already received two thirds of their rewards,

493
00:39:08,865 --> 00:39:15,224
while an army that loses feels fear, and is hurt, have their entire award reserved for them.

494
00:39:15,857 --> 00:39:16,571
This is in Muslim(ألمسلم).

495
00:39:16,963 --> 00:39:21,957
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) in islam, it's a win, win situation! No matter how you look at it, you can't lose.

496
00:39:23,370 --> 00:39:27,033
If you win, your Ajr(أجْر) goes down, but you have won.

497
00:39:27,767 --> 00:39:32,183
And if you lose and you feel fear, you end up getting more Ajr(أجْر) on the Day of Judgment,

498
00:39:32,223 --> 00:39:37,069
so it makes it difficult for you to determine whether you want to win or lose, because you're winning both ways.

499
00:39:39,115 --> 00:39:42,069
And that's the part that drives the enemy crazy,

500
00:39:42,637 --> 00:39:46,041
because the enemy knows that no matter what they do to you, you're happy with it.

501
00:39:47,772 --> 00:39:50,126
I was reading in the paper.

502
00:39:50,678 --> 00:39:55,222
I was in this country when the Amrozi(أمروزي) thing happened, they sentenced him to death.

503
00:39:56,318 --> 00:40:02,686
They cheered, the family of the victims they cheered when he was sentenced to death.

504
00:40:03,506 --> 00:40:06,635
But then when they saw him, two thumbs up and smiling and laughing.

505
00:40:07,126 --> 00:40:09,066
They came out of the court and they changed their mind.

506
00:40:09,146 --> 00:40:10,643
They said: No! We don't want him to die.

507
00:40:11,736 --> 00:40:15,767
They actually did some interviews with some of them and said we would change our mind, we don't want him to die.

508
00:40:16,648 --> 00:40:19,991
Because they see that the man is happy he was actually given what he wants

509
00:40:21,841 --> 00:40:25,852
and with the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم with their enemy.

510
00:40:26,461 --> 00:40:32,250
The enemy eventually got tired of fighting with the Sahabah(صحابه) because the Sahabah(صحابه) are very happy with what they're doing.

511
00:40:33,606 --> 00:40:37,802
While, but because the enemy is doing it for a worldly reason they can only go so far.

512
00:40:38,789 --> 00:40:44,229
Because Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) is temporary, and therefore they want the fast result, but the Sahabah(صحابه) were looking at Aakhirah(آخِرة).

513
00:40:44,293 --> 00:40:46,407
We don't mind if we have to fight for all of our lives.

514
00:40:47,839 --> 00:40:50,942
The virtues of standing in the ranks on the battlefield.

515
00:40:51,758 --> 00:40:54,439
Now going back to the statement of Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه).

516
00:40:55,247 --> 00:40:56,140
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) said:

517
00:40:56,274 --> 00:40:57,251
جنتي في صدري

518
00:40:58,297 --> 00:40:59,580
My Jannah, is in my Jannah(جنة) is in my heart.

519
00:41:00,157 --> 00:41:02,007
سجني عبادتي

520
00:41:03,019 --> 00:41:05,912
If they put me in jail. I will worship Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

521
00:41:07,095 --> 00:41:08,256
ونفعي سياحة

522
00:41:08,970 --> 00:41:12,752
And if they exile me, I will contemplate in the creation of Allah.

523
00:41:13,516 --> 00:41:14,562
وقتلي شهادة

524
00:41:15,042 --> 00:41:17,195
 If they kill me. It's a Shahadah(شَهَادَة) for me.

525
00:41:17,502 --> 00:41:18,862
فما بيفعل عدائ بي

526
00:41:18,931 --> 00:41:19,759
What can my enemy do with me?

527
00:41:21,402 --> 00:41:24,245
No matter what the enemy does, I'll take advantage of it.

528
00:41:27,443 --> 00:41:29,916
The virtue of standing in the ranks on the battlefield.

529
00:41:29,955 --> 00:41:31,252
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says,

530
00:41:31,744 --> 00:41:39,067
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِهِ صَفًّا

531
00:41:39,350 --> 00:41:45,041
صَفًّا كَأَنَّهُم بُنيانٌ مَرصوصٌ

532
00:41:45,471 --> 00:41:52,080
Allah loves those, who fight in His cause in a row, as though they are a single structure, joined firmly.

533
00:41:52,487 --> 00:41:53,950
This is in As-Saff(ألصف) verse four.

534
00:41:54,306 --> 00:41:59,436
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِهِ صَفًّا كَأَنَّهُم بُنيانٌ مَرصوصٌ

535
00:42:00,971 --> 00:42:05,752
Sahal Ibn Saad Sadie(سهل إبن سعد ألساعدي) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

536
00:42:07,012 --> 00:42:10,265
There are two moments when Allah opens the gates of the heavens.

537
00:42:10,767 --> 00:42:15,004
And when that happens, hardly ever would the prayer be rejected.

538
00:42:15,395 --> 00:42:19,577
During the call to prayer, and when the armies line up in their ranks.

539
00:42:20,632 --> 00:42:23,530
And this is in Sunan Abi Daud(سنن إبن أبي داؤد).

540
00:42:25,315 --> 00:42:27,625
In Al-Jamiah(ألجامع) Ibn e Umar(إبن عمر) said:

541
00:42:28,548 --> 00:42:33,768
To stand in the ranks, facing the enemy, even without me striking my sword,

542
00:42:34,203 --> 00:42:41,720
throwing my spear or shooting my arrows is better to me than worshiping Allah for 60 years and not committing any sin.

543
00:42:43,031 --> 00:42:49,922
Just standing there, without doing anything is better than the Ibadah(عبادة) of 60 years.

544
00:42:51,356 --> 00:42:54,778
Imran Ibn Haseen(عمران إبن حصين) narrated the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

545
00:42:55,705 --> 00:43:01,669
Standing in the ranks of the army in the battlefield is better to Allah, than the worship of 60 years.

546
00:43:02,160 --> 00:43:05,490
And this is in Al-Hakim(ألحاكم) and its authentic according to the rules of Bukhari(بخاريْ).

547
00:43:05,704 --> 00:43:08,687
And that's also agreed upon by Az-Zuhri(ألزهري).

548
00:43:09,037 --> 00:43:10,132
So this Hadith(حديث) is Sahih(صحيح).

549
00:43:10,554 --> 00:43:17,746
So with this leverage, you can basically end up on the Day of Judgment, having 500, 600, 700 years of Ibadah(عبادة) on your scale,

550
00:43:18,564 --> 00:43:23,338
depending on how many times you stood in that battle before it actually happened.

551
00:43:24,404 --> 00:43:26,744
It is talking about the serious leverage that you have.

552
00:43:27,039 --> 00:43:30,036
Yazeed Bin Shajara(يذيد بن شجرة), a companion, he said:

553
00:43:30,734 --> 00:43:33,805
I was told that the swords are keys to paradise.

554
00:43:34,342 --> 00:43:41,780
And this is narrated by Abdur Razzaq(عبدالرزاق) with an authentic chain to Yazeed(يذيد), and Yazeed(يذيد) again is a companion.

555
00:43:42,084 --> 00:43:46,999
So he said: I was told that, the swords are keys to paradise.

556
00:43:47,471 --> 00:43:53,122
Now if we're going to take these words as figurative to personal arms.

557
00:43:54,009 --> 00:43:58,342
One can also say that the whenever you see somebody with an AK-47, that's the key to Jannah(جنة),

558
00:43:59,136 --> 00:44:05,973
because the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ needs to be taken in the general sense, and not limited to a certain time.

559
00:44:06,553 --> 00:44:12,504
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was talking to Sahabah رضي الله عنهم according to the terminology that they can understand.

560
00:44:14,267 --> 00:44:20,259
Just as the sword was the predominant weapon, in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

561
00:44:21,072 --> 00:44:24,145
the Kalashankov(کلاشنکوف) is the predominant weapon around the world today.

562
00:44:24,695 --> 00:44:32,481
And there was an article I think it was in the dependent on the time that 200 million rifles were produced.

563
00:44:33,743 --> 00:44:34,931
Abdullah Ibn Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو) said:

564
00:44:35,551 --> 00:44:40,939
Should I tell you about the best martyr on the Day of Judgment, that is the one who stands in the ranks on the battlefield.

565
00:44:41,673 --> 00:44:46,865
And when they face the enemy he does not turn left or right, rather he carries his sword and says,

566
00:44:47,305 --> 00:44:53,338
O Allah, today I hand over to You my soul to make up for my past days.

567
00:44:54,370 --> 00:44:55,228
And then he is killed.

568
00:44:56,403 --> 00:45:02,515
That person is among the martyrs, who now lay down in the high rooms of paradise, wherever they wish.

569
00:45:03,436 --> 00:45:04,752
Abdullah Ibn Amr(عبدالله بن عمرو) said:

570
00:45:05,222 --> 00:45:08,132
Shall I tell you about the best martyr on the Day of Judgment?

571
00:45:08,594 --> 00:45:13,585
That is the one, who stands in the ranks on the battlefield and when they face the enemy,

572
00:45:14,091 --> 00:45:18,653
he does not turn left or right, rather he carries his sword and says:

573
00:45:18,752 --> 00:45:24,075
O Allah, today I hand over to you my soul, to make up for my past days.

574
00:45:24,891 --> 00:45:27,208
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), this is the At-Toba(التوبة).

575
00:45:27,843 --> 00:45:33,595
O Allah! I'm coming to you with my sword, so forgive me for my past days,

576
00:45:34,251 --> 00:45:41,603
and then he is killed, that person is among the martyrs, who now lay down in the high rooms of paradise wherever he wished.

577
00:45:42,481 --> 00:45:45,038
A chapter on the farewell of fighters.

578
00:45:47,247 --> 00:45:51,338
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه escorting in, an army and walked with them and then he said:

579
00:45:51,442 --> 00:45:54,924
Praise be to Allah for having dust on our feet in His cause.

580
00:45:55,112 --> 00:45:55,833
The man said:

581
00:45:56,442 --> 00:45:58,713
But we just escorted them and gave them farewell.

582
00:45:59,881 --> 00:46:00,709
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said:

583
00:46:02,425 --> 00:46:08,872
Allah is praised, because we have accumulated dust on our feet Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

584
00:46:10,828 --> 00:46:15,735
Now because we said that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and the early Muslims considered Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) to be Jihad(جهاد).

585
00:46:16,603 --> 00:46:18,643
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was questioned about that statement.

586
00:46:18,763 --> 00:46:23,746
How can you say that you have your feet, dusty in the path of Allah,

587
00:46:23,910 --> 00:46:29,752
when you just walked out with them to the outskirts of Madina, he didn't really go out with them to the battlefield.

588
00:46:29,981 --> 00:46:34,234
So it also shows you that their understanding of Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله) was Al-Qital(ألقتال).

589
00:46:34,899 --> 00:46:38,471
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه responded by saying we prepared them.

590
00:46:39,096 --> 00:46:42,150
We gave them farewell, and we made prayers for them.

591
00:46:43,604 --> 00:46:47,473
Because we are giving them Wada'ah(وداع), we are giving them farewell.

592
00:46:48,246 --> 00:46:50,101
It's counts as being Sabeel-Lillah(سَبيل الله).

593
00:46:50,567 --> 00:46:57,842
In other words, giving farewell to them Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), when they're leaving, and giving them that moral support,

594
00:46:58,436 --> 00:47:00,413
counts as being Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

595
00:47:02,962 --> 00:47:05,532
The next chapter, very important:

596
00:47:07,412 --> 00:47:11,476
The virtues of spending in the cause of Allah. And this is chapter three.

597
00:47:12,607 --> 00:47:17,806
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says, Surah Baqarah(سورة البقرة) verse, 245:

598
00:47:19,110 --> 00:47:30,415
مَن ذَا الَّذي يُقرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرضًا حَسَنًا فَيُضاعِفَهُ لَهُ أَضعافًا كَثيرَةً ۚ

599
00:47:31,221 --> 00:47:37,099
وَاللَّهُ يَقبِضُ وَيَبسُطُ وَإِلَيهِ تُرجَعونَ۞

600
00:47:38,429 --> 00:47:41,128
Who is it that would loan, Allah a goodly loan.

601
00:47:41,852 --> 00:47:45,213
So He may multiply it for him many times over.

602
00:47:45,775 --> 00:47:51,525
And it is Allah, Who withholds and grants and abundance, and to Him you will be returned.

603
00:47:52,393 --> 00:47:53,459
The Ayah(آية) is,

604
00:47:53,717 --> 00:47:55,749
مَن ذَا الَّذي يُقرِضُ اللَّهَ قَرضًا حَسَنًا

605
00:47:56,350 --> 00:48:02,355
فَيُضاعِفَهُ لَهُ أَضعافًا كَثيرَةً ۚ وَاللَّهُ يَقبِضُ وَيَبسُطُ وَإِلَيهِ تُرجَعونَ۞

606
00:48:02,588 --> 00:48:04,598
Verse 261in Surah Baqarah(سورة البقرة).

607
00:48:04,801 --> 00:48:12,801
مَثَلُ الَّذينَ يُنفِقونَ أَموالَهُم في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ

608
00:48:13,801 --> 00:48:22,713
 كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ أَنبَتَت سَبعَ سَنابِلَ في كُلِّ سُنبُلَةٍ مِائَةُ حَبَّةٍ ۗ

609
00:48:23,017 --> 00:48:28,883
وَاللَّهُ يُضاعِفُ لِمَن يَشاءُ ۗ

610
00:48:29,166 --> 00:48:32,888
وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ عَليمٌ ۞

611
00:48:33,089 --> 00:48:42,156
The example of those, who spend their wealth in the way of Allah, is like a seed which grows seven spikes in each spike is 100 grains.

612
00:48:42,603 --> 00:48:47,330
And Allah multipliers for Whom, He wills and Allah is all encompassing and knowing.

613
00:48:48,173 --> 00:48:53,252
مَثَلُ الَّذينَ يُنفِقونَ أَموالَهُم في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ كَمَثَلِ حَبَّةٍ أَنبَتَت سَبعَ سَنابِلَ

614
00:48:53,714 --> 00:49:00,246
في كُلِّ سُنبُلَةٍ مِائَةُ حَبَّةٍ ۗ وَاللَّهُ يُضاعِفُ لِمَن يَشاءُ ۗ وَاللَّهُ واسِعٌ عَليمٌ۞

615
00:49:01,869 --> 00:49:03,775
 How many times is the Hasana(حسنة) multiplied?

616
00:49:05,564 --> 00:49:07,659
بِٱلْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهُۥ عَشْرُ أَمْثَالِهَا ۖ

617
00:49:07,684 --> 00:49:07,828
Right!

618
00:49:08,822 --> 00:49:12,561
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: In Qur'an that one good deed is multiplied by 10.

619
00:49:14,485 --> 00:49:16,823
How come in this Ayah(آية), it says 700?

620
00:49:21,939 --> 00:49:22,454
What's the reason?

621
00:49:27,320 --> 00:49:31,090
No! This is 700, and that's 10.!

622
00:49:32,409 --> 00:49:34,360
How come Qur'an says in one Ayah(آية),

623
00:49:34,400 --> 00:49:35,814
بِٱلْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهُۥ عَشْرُ أَمْثَالِهَا ۖ

624
00:49:36,166 --> 00:49:37,750
And in this Ayah(آية), it is 700.

625
00:49:39,947 --> 00:49:42,056
Because this Ayah(آية) is talking about Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

626
00:49:43,355 --> 00:49:47,656
Therefore, in general, the good deed is multiplied by 10.

627
00:49:48,235 --> 00:49:55,049
But when the Infaaq(إنفاق), the spending is in the path of Allah Al-Jihad(جهاد), it is 700.

628
00:49:56,186 --> 00:50:02,108
Therefore the Nafaqah(نفقة) that goes, Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), is 700,

629
00:50:02,426 --> 00:50:06,225
while the Nafaqah(نفقة) that goes in other branches of Infaaq(إنفاق) is 10,

630
00:50:08,996 --> 00:50:15,100
قال مدخول يعني ألإنفاق في الجهاد من الرباط الخيل وعداد السلاح وغير ذالك

631
00:50:15,180 --> 00:50:23,457
Author says, what is meant here and this is spending in Jihad(جهاد), like for horses, and for weapons and other issues,

632
00:50:23,556 --> 00:50:24,611
and Al-Qurtabi(ألقرطبي) says:

633
00:50:24,914 --> 00:50:29,800
ورد القرآن بأن الحسنة في جميع أعمال البر بعشر أمثالها ،

634
00:50:30,137 --> 00:50:34,974
واقتضت هذه الآية أن نفقة الجهاد حسنتها بسبعمائة ضعف

635
00:50:35,674 --> 00:50:41,872
Al-Qurtabi(ألقرطبي) says Qur'an says that one Hasana(حسنة) is multiplied by 10 in every other good deed.

636
00:50:42,165 --> 00:50:49,246
But this Ayah(آية) shows us that spending specifically in Jihad(جهاد), the one good deed is multiplied by 700.

637
00:50:49,806 --> 00:50:52,562
So these are the words of Al-Qurtabi(ألقرطبي).

638
00:50:54,392 --> 00:50:58,519
Ibn Asakir(إبن عساكر), he has one paragraph about the Anfaaq(أنفاق) of the Sahabah(صحابه), I'll just read it.

639
00:50:58,674 --> 00:51:05,138
وحضر رسول الله المسلمين على الجهادورغَّبهم فيه وامرهم بالصدقة ، فحملوا صدقات كثيرة،

640
00:51:05,628 --> 00:51:11,285
وكان اول من حمل ابوبكر الصديق بماله كله أربعة آلاف درهم

641
00:51:11,733 --> 00:51:14,929
فقال له صلى الله عليه وسلم هل أبقيت لأهلك  شَيْئًا؟

642
00:51:15,395 --> 00:51:17,277
فقال: الله ورسوله أعلم

643
00:51:17,347 --> 00:51:20,773
وفي رواية ما وعد الله ورسوله من الرزق خير،

644
00:51:21,081 --> 00:51:24,036
و في رواية أبقيت له من الله ورسوله

645
00:51:24,643 --> 00:51:28,574
Rasool Allah ﷺ encourage the Muslims to give and this was in Tabook(تبوك).

646
00:51:29,121 --> 00:51:32,462
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) came with all of his wealth 400 Dirham,

647
00:51:32,874 --> 00:51:36,147
so Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, did you leave anything behind for your family.?

648
00:51:36,520 --> 00:51:40,240
He said: Allah and His Messenger, know best and in another narration,

649
00:51:40,296 --> 00:51:43,899
he said: What Allah and His Messenger promised is better.

650
00:51:46,288 --> 00:51:51,069
And in another narration, he said: I left them, Allah and His Messenger, meaning he gave everything.

651
00:51:53,151 --> 00:51:58,036
ثم جاء عمر بنصف ماله فقال له صلى الله عليه وسلم هل أبقيت لأهلك شَيْئًا؟

652
00:51:58,125 --> 00:51:59,386
 قال نصف ما جئت به

653
00:52:00,193 --> 00:52:02,467
And then Umar(عُمَر) came, and Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him:

654
00:52:02,560 --> 00:52:04,443
What did you leave for your family?

655
00:52:04,667 --> 00:52:07,437
He said: I left them half of my wealth.

656
00:52:08,528 --> 00:52:12,072
But then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), He knew that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) came ahead of him.

657
00:52:12,112 --> 00:52:16,948
He said: I have never raced Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in anything but he would come ahead of me.

658
00:52:18,698 --> 00:52:22,401
Umar(عُمَر)'s intention was to beat Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to it first.

659
00:52:23,057 --> 00:52:32,305
See Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), he would just do these good deeds and maybe he didn't really have on mind, competing with others, it was himself.

660
00:52:33,103 --> 00:52:37,632
That's how he was, but because he was the best everybody else was trying to compete with him.

661
00:52:38,082 --> 00:52:40,164
It was the others who are trying to catch up with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

662
00:52:40,939 --> 00:52:42,283
not the other way around.

663
00:52:42,717 --> 00:52:43,343
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) he just do it,

664
00:52:43,469 --> 00:52:47,269
مَنْ لِي بِمِثْلِ مَشِّكَل الْمُدَلَّلِ تَمْشِي رُوَيْدًا وَتَجِي الْأَوَّلِ

665
00:52:47,828 --> 00:52:48,948
It's line of poetry, it says:

666
00:52:49,630 --> 00:52:52,788
 Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه it was his natural self,

667
00:52:55,159 --> 00:53:00,259
the Messenger of Allah said: Whoever spends in the path of Allah, it would be multiplied for them 700 times.

668
00:53:00,371 --> 00:53:03,584
So, this is a Hadith(حديث) that specifically points to Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

669
00:53:04,056 --> 00:53:07,607
It's in At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ), Nasai(نسائ), Ibn Habban(إبن حبان), Al-Hakam(الحاكم), and Al-Ahmad(ألأحمد) and its authentic.

670
00:53:09,595 --> 00:53:11,609
A man came to Rasool Allah ﷺ with a camel.

671
00:53:12,086 --> 00:53:16,653
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You will be given 700 camels similar to it on the day of judgment.

672
00:53:17,909 --> 00:53:21,903
Therefore, when you drop that pound.

673
00:53:24,181 --> 00:53:27,090
You'll be given 700 pounds on the day of judgment.

674
00:53:28,429 --> 00:53:33,995
You dropped the keys to your car, you would be given 700 brand new cars on the day of judgment.

675
00:53:35,272 --> 00:53:37,944
Whatever you drop will be multiplied by 700.

676
00:53:39,146 --> 00:53:41,322
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريره) narrated, the Messenger of Allah said:

677
00:53:41,415 --> 00:53:46,257
Whoever spends a pair in the cause of Allah would be called on the day of judgment to enter into paradise.

678
00:53:46,865 --> 00:53:49,199
The people of prayer will be called from the gate of prayer,

679
00:53:49,502 --> 00:53:52,026
the people of Jihad(جهاد) will be called from the gate of Jihad(جهاد),

680
00:53:52,321 --> 00:53:55,018
the people of Sadaqah(صدقة) will be called from the gate of Sadaqah(صدقة),

681
00:53:55,288 --> 00:53:58,657
and the people of fasting would be called from the gate called Ar-Rayyan(ألريان).

682
00:53:59,385 --> 00:54:00,385
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said:

683
00:54:00,857 --> 00:54:03,871
Would there be anyone who would be called from all of those gates,

684
00:54:04,162 --> 00:54:06,441
the Messenger of Allah said: Yes! And you are one of them.

685
00:54:07,580 --> 00:54:09,971
This is in Ahmad(أحمد), Bukhari(بخاريْ), Muslim(ألمسلم) and in An-Nasai(ألنَّسائي).

686
00:54:13,120 --> 00:54:14,679
SaaSah Bin Muavia(صعصعة بن معاوية) said:

687
00:54:14,730 --> 00:54:17,400
I went to Abu Dhar(ابوزر)'s house and I didn't find him,

688
00:54:17,899 --> 00:54:18,767
He was one of Tabieen(تابعين).

689
00:54:19,740 --> 00:54:26,926
I then met him coming back with a camel with water on its back for his house, I asked him: Are you Abu Dhar(ابوزر)?

690
00:54:27,579 --> 00:54:30,162
Abu Dhar(ابوزر) said that's what my family, call me.

691
00:54:33,369 --> 00:54:37,151
He said: Can you narrate to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah.

692
00:54:37,658 --> 00:54:39,648
So that's Allah may benefit me from it.

693
00:54:40,900 --> 00:54:41,721
Abu Dhar(ابوزر) said:

694
00:54:42,501 --> 00:54:49,373
 Whoever spends a pair in the cause of Allah will have the gatekeepers of paradise rushing towards him on the day of judgment,

695
00:54:49,898 --> 00:54:52,897
competing on who would be the one to invite him,

696
00:54:53,488 --> 00:54:57,930
I said what is a pair, he said, a pair of horses, or a pair of camels.

697
00:54:59,433 --> 00:55:01,529
And this is in Al-Hakim(ألحاكم), Ahmad(أحمد) and An-Nasai(ألنسائ).

698
00:55:04,262 --> 00:55:06,326
Soban(ثعبان) narrated the Messenger of Allah said:

699
00:55:07,000 --> 00:55:11,776
The best dinar(دينار) you could spend is the one, you spend on your family,

700
00:55:12,406 --> 00:55:15,288
the dinar(دينار) you spend on your mount, in the cause of Allah

701
00:55:15,637 --> 00:55:18,679
and the dinar(دينار) you spend on your companions in the cause of Allah.

702
00:55:20,090 --> 00:55:21,586
Muhib Ud-Din At-Tabri(محب الدين ألطبري) said:

703
00:55:22,555 --> 00:55:25,686
I think I mentioned this to you before about Tabook(تبوك).

704
00:55:25,761 --> 00:55:29,875
Uthman(عثمان) first came with 300 camels full with their saddles.

705
00:55:30,170 --> 00:55:32,800
Then he came with 1000 gold dinars.

706
00:55:32,849 --> 00:55:39,047
Then he saw that, the army is still short, so he brought in horses and camels up to a total of 1000.

707
00:55:39,761 --> 00:55:44,594
When that wasn't enough, he sent in 10,000 dinars, with 20 horses.

708
00:55:45,819 --> 00:55:47,962
A few points regarding the issue of Nafaqa(نفقة).

709
00:55:49,888 --> 00:56:00,529
Muslim accepts the path of struggle as their path, intellectually, they agree with the idea of it,

710
00:56:01,649 --> 00:56:03,765
but because they're far away from the events.

711
00:56:04,687 --> 00:56:07,566
It remains as an intellectual activity to them.

712
00:56:10,578 --> 00:56:16,510
What happens is if the brothers stay just talking about the issue of Jihad(جهاد).

713
00:56:17,608 --> 00:56:21,934
For too long, they end up talking about it, only.

714
00:56:23,820 --> 00:56:31,647
It carries on and on and on, and what happens is, a person accepts that state as being appropriate.

715
00:56:32,591 --> 00:56:33,525
And it just carries on.

716
00:56:35,117 --> 00:56:40,490
So the whole issue becomes an intellectual discourse, and doesn't go beyond that.

717
00:56:42,276 --> 00:56:44,934
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), the Ayah(آية) that talked about,

718
00:56:45,150 --> 00:56:52,401
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا لِمَ تَقولونَ ما لا تَفعَلونَ ۞

719
00:56:53,066 --> 00:56:59,696
كَبُرَ مَقتًا عِندَ اللَّهِ أَن تَقولوا ما لا تَفعَلونَ ۞

720
00:57:00,269 --> 00:57:07,659
إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِهِ صَفًّا

721
00:57:07,878 --> 00:57:13,529
صَفًّا كَأَنَّهُم بُنيانٌ مَرصوصٌ۞

722
00:57:13,901 --> 00:57:19,563
 Oh, you who believe, why do you say what you don't do, was specifically talking about this issue.

723
00:57:21,989 --> 00:57:25,374
That was the Sabab(سبب) of Nazool(نزول), that was the reason, why the Ayah(آية) was revealed.

724
00:57:25,612 --> 00:57:27,822
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا لِمَ تَقولونَ ما لا تَفعَلونَ ۞

725
00:57:28,637 --> 00:57:30,949
 كَبُرَ مَقتًا عِندَ اللَّهِ أَن تَقولوا ما لا تَفعَلونَ ۞

726
00:57:31,023 --> 00:57:35,556
إنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الَّذينَ يُقاتِلونَ في سَبيلِهِ صَفًّا كَأَنَّهُم بُنيانٌ مَرصوصٌ۞

727
00:57:35,626 --> 00:57:37,808
Allah loves the ones, who fight in His path, not talking about the fight.

728
00:57:38,275 --> 00:57:39,233
The ones who actually fight.

729
00:57:39,705 --> 00:57:47,027
Brothers who have been talking about the issue of Hijrah(هجرة) and the issue of going to fight for years, years, and nothing is changing.

730
00:57:47,501 --> 00:57:49,650
It's just intentions and talks.

731
00:57:49,938 --> 00:57:54,168
And sometimes one might justify to themselves that this Hadith(حديث) says,

732
00:57:54,218 --> 00:57:58,291
مَنْ مَاتَ وَلَمْ يَغْزُ وَلَمْ يُحَدِّثْ نَفْسَهُ بِهِ؛ مَاتَ عَلَى شُعْبَةٍ مِنْ نِفَاقٍ

733
00:57:58,963 --> 00:58:03,180
If you don't make Ghazoo(غزؤ) or make the intentions of it then you're dying as on a branch of Nifaq(نِفاق),

734
00:58:03,544 --> 00:58:05,405
that at least I'm making the intentions of it,

735
00:58:05,856 --> 00:58:06,782
but keep in mind

736
00:58:07,731 --> 00:58:12,555
that this Hadith(حديث) is talking about making intentions to the Ghazoo(غزؤ) that is Fardh Kifaya(فرض كفاية), not Fardh Ain(فرض عين)

737
00:58:12,730 --> 00:58:14,856
وَلَوْ أَرَادُواْ ٱلْخُرُوجَ لَأَعَدُّواْ لَهُۥ عُدَّةً

738
00:58:15,006 --> 00:58:17,587
If they want to set out, they would have prepared for it.

739
00:58:17,955 --> 00:58:23,585
Remember we talked about this Ayah(آية), the issue of being ready and prepared afore time.

740
00:58:25,374 --> 00:58:29,386
Again having the Niyyah(نية) alone is not sufficient when it's Farz Ain(فرض عين) and Farz Ain(فرض عين) must be done.

741
00:58:29,857 --> 00:58:33,361
 It's not enough just to say that I have the attention so I'm, free of Nifaq(نِفاق).

742
00:58:33,636 --> 00:58:37,241
We have to be clear, because Jihad(جهاد), allot of confusion happens,

743
00:58:37,292 --> 00:58:41,606
if one doesn't differentiate between the Jihad(جهاد) that is Fardh Kifaya(فرض كفاية), and the jihad that is Farz Ain(فرض عين).

744
00:58:42,658 --> 00:58:47,232
I mean, every Nas(نص) would have a meaning according to whether it is Farz Ain(فرض عين) or Fardh Kifaya(فرض كفاية),

745
00:58:47,930 --> 00:58:53,268
And Jihad(جهاد) become Farz Ain(فرض عين) according to Ibn Qudama(إبن قدامة) in three circumstances.

746
00:58:53,765 --> 00:58:57,846
Number one, when the enemy lands on your land.

747
00:58:59,220 --> 00:59:03,495
Number two, when the Imam(اِمَام) recruits the soldiers.

748
00:59:04,245 --> 00:59:06,518
And number three, when the Army's meet.

749
00:59:07,335 --> 00:59:12,491
So when the armies meet, even if it is a Jihad(جهاد) that is Fardh Kifaya(فرض كفاية) it is too late to bail out,

750
00:59:12,871 --> 00:59:14,859
you made the decision to be there, you have to hang on.

751
00:59:15,294 --> 00:59:25,388
Why are we talking about making Hijrah(هجرة) or going to fight out when you can fulfill at least half of the Farz Ain(فرض عين)

752
00:59:25,784 --> 00:59:26,853
straight from your pocket,

753
00:59:27,401 --> 00:59:31,972
because, as Al-Jihad(ألجهاد), Jihadaan(جهادان) Jihad bilmaal(جهاد بالمال) Wa Jihad Bin Nafs(جهاد بالنفس).

754
00:59:33,417 --> 00:59:39,428
Jihad(جهاد), there's two types of it, one with the Nafs(نفس) and one with the money.

755
00:59:40,020 --> 00:59:45,690
So there is no excuse about talking about it and carrying on talking about it when the opportunity to act upon it,

756
00:59:45,907 --> 00:59:48,138
all what it needs is for you to stick your hand in your pocket.

757
00:59:48,835 --> 00:59:50,291
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه), he says:

758
00:59:50,732 --> 00:59:53,451
 وَمَنْ عَجَزَ عَنْ الْجِهَادِ بِبَدَنِهِ

759
00:59:53,854 --> 00:59:57,246
وَقَدَرَ عَلَى الْجِهَادِ بِمَالِهِ وَجَبَ عَلَيْهِ الْجِهَادُ بِمَالِهِ

760
00:59:58,375 --> 01:00:00,724
وَهُوَ نَصُّ أَحْمَدَ فِي رِوَايَةِ أَبِي الْحَكَمِ

761
01:00:01,140 --> 01:00:03,815
وَهُوَ الَّذِي قَطَعَ بِهِ الْقَاضِي فِي أَحْكَامِ الْقُرْآنِ

762
01:00:04,625 --> 01:00:07,709
فِي سُورَةِ بَرَاءَةٌ عِنْدَ قَوْلِهِ: {انْفِرُوا خِفَافًا وَثِقَالا} [التوبة: 41]

763
01:00:08,312 --> 01:00:11,512
فَيَجِبُ عَلَى الْمُوسِرِينَ النَّفَقَةُ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ

764
01:00:11,853 --> 01:00:16,992
وَعَلَى هَذَا فَيَجِبُ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ الْجِهَادُ فِي أَمْوَالِهِنَّ إنْ كَانَ فِيهَا

765
01:00:17,682 --> 01:00:18,666
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says:

766
01:00:19,836 --> 01:00:23,595
If a person is unable to make jihad(جهاد) with their body,

767
01:00:24,480 --> 01:00:30,666
and they are able to make Jihad(جهاد) with the money that it becomes Farz(فرض), Wajib(واجب) on him to do so.

768
01:00:31,202 --> 01:00:35,640
And that is what Ahmad Ibn Hanbal(أحمد إبن حنبل) stated in the narration of Abul Hakam(أبوالحكم).

769
01:00:36,248 --> 01:00:41,447
And it is the opinion of Al-Qazi Abu Bakr Al-Arbi(ألقاضي ابوبكرألعربي) in Ahkaam Ul Quran(ألإحكام القرآن),

770
01:00:41,487 --> 01:00:43,541
when he talked about the Tafseer(تفسير) of Ayah(آية)

771
01:00:43,665 --> 01:00:45,085
انْفِرُوا خِفَافًا وَثِقَالا

772
01:00:45,157 --> 01:00:46,484
Set out light and heavy.

773
01:00:47,211 --> 01:00:48,558
And then Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says:

774
01:00:49,757 --> 01:00:56,609
So it is mandatory on the wealthy to spend in the path of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

775
01:00:57,117 --> 01:01:01,810
and it is even mandatory on the women to give out if they have additional money.

776
01:01:02,711 --> 01:01:08,305
If their women have more than their necessary needs, it becomes Wajib(واجب) upon them to give out.

777
01:01:09,478 --> 01:01:13,176
Now, these statements are not in your notes to one by Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) and Ibn Qayyim(إبن قيم)

778
01:01:13,450 --> 01:01:16,775
and so you might to want to jot them down.

779
01:01:16,859 --> 01:01:19,724
Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبن ألقيم). He says, and this is in Zad ul Maad(زادالمعاد),

780
01:01:20,646 --> 01:01:26,072
ومنها يعني فقه هذه غزوة وجوب الجهاد بالمال كما يجب جهاد بالنفس

781
01:01:26,648 --> 01:01:31,983
Ibn Qayyim(إبن قيم) says and one of the lessons we learned is that Jihad(جهاد) through your wealth is mandatory

782
01:01:32,031 --> 01:01:34,789
just like it's mandatory to make Jihad Bin Nafs(جهادبالنفس).

783
01:01:35,317 --> 01:01:37,618
And this is one of the narrations from Ahmad(أحمد),

784
01:01:37,905 --> 01:01:39,705
وهو إحدى الروايتين عن أحمد وهي الصواب الذي لا ريب فيه

785
01:01:39,983 --> 01:01:41,402
And it is certainly the truth.

786
01:01:42,412 --> 01:01:47,149
فإن الأمر بالجهاد بالمال شقيق الأمر بالجهاد بالنفس

787
01:01:47,229 --> 01:01:53,372
في القرآن وقرينه بل جاء مقدما على الجهاد بالنفس في كل موضع إلا موضعا واحدا

788
01:01:54,228 --> 01:02:01,992
He says: Because Jihad(جهاد) of money is the twin of Jihad(جهاد) of the body in Qur'an,

789
01:02:02,512 --> 01:02:04,417
and it is always mentioned with it.

790
01:02:04,556 --> 01:02:10,135
In fact, it always comes before the Jihad(جهاد) of the body except in one Ayah(آية),

791
01:02:11,355 --> 01:02:17,069
In every single Ayah(آية) in Qur'an. It starts with money before the Nafs(نفس), with the exception of the Ayah(آية).

792
01:02:17,105 --> 01:02:20,718
إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱشْتَرَىٰ مِنَ ٱلْمُؤْمِنِينَ أَنفُسَهُمْ وَأَمْوَٰلَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ ٱلْجَنَّةَ ۚ

793
01:02:21,234 --> 01:02:23,092
So then Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبن القيم) says,

794
01:02:23,568 --> 01:02:29,078
وهذا يدل على أن الجهاد به أهم وآكد من الجهاد بالنفس

795
01:02:29,666 --> 01:02:37,123
He says and this is an evidence that Jihad(جهاد) of the wealth is more important than the Jihad(جهاد) of the soul, and more emphasized,

796
01:02:37,647 --> 01:02:39,230
ولا ريب أنه أحد الجهادين

797
01:02:39,266 --> 01:02:41,749
And there's no doubt that it's one of the two Jihads.

798
01:02:42,133 --> 01:02:46,127
كما قال النبي صلى الله عليه و سلم : من جهز غازيا فقد غزا

799
01:02:46,404 --> 01:02:49,465
That whoever finances a fighter has actually fought.

800
01:02:50,269 --> 01:02:53,831
فيجب على القادر عليه كما يجب على القادر بالبدن

801
01:02:54,159 --> 01:02:56,285
It  is mandatory to the one, who can do it,

802
01:02:56,448 --> 01:02:59,645
just like it's mandatory to  the one, who can fight for this body to do it.

803
01:03:01,079 --> 01:03:04,240
ولا يتم الجهاد بالبدن إلا ببذله

804
01:03:05,161 --> 01:03:11,193
ولا ينتصر إلا بالعدد والعدد فإن لم يقدر أن يكثر العدد

805
01:03:11,504 --> 01:03:19,264
وجب عليه أن يمد بالمال والعدة وإذا وجب الحج بالمال على العاجز بالبدن فوجوب الجهاد بالمال أولى وأحرى

806
01:03:20,335 --> 01:03:25,521
He says: Just like it becomes mandatory on the person who cannot physically go to Hajj(حَجْ)

807
01:03:26,057 --> 01:03:28,824
to finance somebody who will make Hajj(حَجْ) instead of him,

808
01:03:29,168 --> 01:03:35,187
it becomes mandatory, on the one, who cannot make Jihad(جهاد) by their body to make Jihad(جهاد) through their wealth.

809
01:03:36,123 --> 01:03:37,593
One does not have an excuse.

810
01:03:37,673 --> 01:03:41,779
Now, see the danger brothers is, somebody who doesn't understand this concept,

811
01:03:42,803 --> 01:03:44,319
قد جعب جهل يوم القيامة

812
01:03:44,382 --> 01:03:46,620
Could be excused on the day of judgment, because of ignorance.

813
01:03:47,232 --> 01:03:52,532
However, somebody knows the truth, and knows that this is the path that pleases Allah and then doesn't do anything about it.

814
01:03:52,778 --> 01:03:53,359
That's a crime.!

815
01:03:54,898 --> 01:03:56,203
You see the difference between the two.

816
01:03:56,664 --> 01:04:00,825
Somebody who doesn't know about it could be free on the day of judgment

817
01:04:00,896 --> 01:04:04,539
and could be set free and wouldn't be held accountable for that because nobody really talked him about it.

818
01:04:05,400 --> 01:04:10,245
But when you have the information with you and you know the true path, and then nothing happens.

819
01:04:10,805 --> 01:04:14,093
That makes it a disaster because a person who has the knowledge

820
01:04:14,198 --> 01:04:17,649
and then doesn't act upon it is worse than the person who doesn't have the knowledge.

821
01:04:18,474 --> 01:04:20,652
And there's another issue that I need to pay attention to.

822
01:04:22,014 --> 01:04:27,962
The mere existence of a Muslim in the land of Al-Kuffr(ألكفر), according to the principles of Shariah(شريعة) is not allowed.

823
01:04:28,366 --> 01:04:30,588
أنا بريء من كل مسلم يقيم بين أظهر المشركين

824
01:04:31,286 --> 01:04:35,326
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: I am free from the ones, who live among the Mushrikeen(مشركين).

825
01:04:36,004 --> 01:04:40,395
Therefore, the existence of every Muslim needs to be justified.

826
01:04:41,514 --> 01:04:46,054
There needs to be a justification for it, it's not something that is accepted by default,

827
01:04:46,134 --> 01:04:51,346
there must be a reason, just to free the person from the burden of being in a state of sin,

828
01:04:51,912 --> 01:04:55,424
and that is to serve the cause through two ways, Da'wah(دعوة) and money.

829
01:04:56,004 --> 01:04:59,540
Da'wah(دعوة) by conveying the message and money by financing it.

830
01:05:02,892 --> 01:05:05,743
And you'd find that the Rasool Allah ﷺ when he said:

831
01:05:05,965 --> 01:05:09,507
جاهِدُوا المُشرِكينَ بِأَموالِكُمْ وأَنْفُسِكُم وأَلسِنَتِكُم

832
01:05:10,099 --> 01:05:12,734
This is really a concept of total war.

833
01:05:14,139 --> 01:05:20,490
You are fighting against the enemy with your wealth with your money, and with your tongues, even your words.

834
01:05:21,027 --> 01:05:23,920
So everything is geared towards this objective.

835
01:05:27,602 --> 01:05:34,106
We talked previously about when we mentioned the story of the fighter wanted to go on Hajj(حَجْ).

836
01:05:34,970 --> 01:05:36,843
So he went to the Shaikh(شيخ) and he asked him about it.

837
01:05:38,335 --> 01:05:42,408
He said: Because I missed the house of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ I want to go back to it.

838
01:05:42,471 --> 01:05:43,225
What did he tell him.?

839
01:05:43,511 --> 01:05:46,284
He said: You need to do what Allah wants, not what you want.

840
01:05:47,955 --> 01:05:53,321
So whenever we're looking at our situation we need to determine what are the priorities here,

841
01:05:54,289 --> 01:05:56,377
not what I want or feel like doing.

842
01:05:57,090 --> 01:06:02,869
We always have that urge of following what is more appealing to ourselves, but the Ajr(أجْر) is not there.

843
01:06:03,591 --> 01:06:08,905
The Ajr(أجْر) is in doing what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ wants you to do in your place, according to your skills and abilities.

844
01:06:10,085 --> 01:06:15,561
So what are the priorities Yani(يعني) I'll be frank and open about it.

845
01:06:16,262 --> 01:06:19,552
Yani(يعني), somebody brought up on a flat Island

846
01:06:20,007 --> 01:06:23,673
wouldn't really be able to compete with the Pathans, who are living out of their lives on mountains.

847
01:06:25,586 --> 01:06:32,839
There is some natural ability that is given to a person sometimes you're fighting as, you just don't have it.

848
01:06:33,872 --> 01:06:37,181
And some of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were strong in the battlefield, some weren't.

849
01:06:37,237 --> 01:06:39,132
Everybody knew where to put their skills,

850
01:06:40,124 --> 01:06:43,430
someone who starts training at the age of 25 or 30

851
01:06:44,831 --> 01:06:49,775
are not going to be as confident as for example a Yemeni tribesmen who starts playing with these toys at the age of 10.

852
01:06:51,370 --> 01:06:57,389
So, you know, you have to you have to realize what you are able to do what I'm able to do.

853
01:06:57,508 --> 01:07:00,604
Everybody needs to look at their skills and determine what they're best at.

854
01:07:01,199 --> 01:07:03,060
I'm not saying that one should not do this.

855
01:07:03,634 --> 01:07:06,609
Don't get me wrong, there needs to be a bottom line of everything.

856
01:07:07,993 --> 01:07:09,780
But why compete with these people,

857
01:07:09,844 --> 01:07:15,531
Yani(يعني) for example the endurance of the Chechens or the Kashmiris who are living in this difficulty all of their life

858
01:07:16,015 --> 01:07:19,217
 will be different than somebody who's brought up in a very spoiled environment.

859
01:07:22,372 --> 01:07:24,054
However, when you look at it,

860
01:07:26,331 --> 01:07:34,897
the Kashmiri or the Chechen or Afgani, will never even dream of competing with you in the area of Jihad Bil Mal(جهاد بالمال).

861
01:07:36,383 --> 01:07:40,162
The numbers that you can quote, their minds wouldn't even be able to comprehend.

862
01:07:40,718 --> 01:07:44,368
Some of them they live on amounts of money that are unbelievable.

863
01:07:44,638 --> 01:07:48,424
And when you talk about the amount of money that you can give off your salary.

864
01:07:48,713 --> 01:07:50,650
It is something that they wouldn't even make it in a year.

865
01:07:51,173 --> 01:07:54,729
So why play the game with their rules, why not play it with your rules.

866
01:07:54,800 --> 01:07:57,281
With what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has already given you.

867
01:07:59,058 --> 01:08:02,709
Plus we know from the Seerah(سيرة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

868
01:08:03,383 --> 01:08:07,368
that the Sahabah(صحابه) who are able to spend were always ahead of the Sahabah(صحابه) who weren't.

869
01:08:08,248 --> 01:08:12,539
And we know that from the Hadith(حديث) of the poor Sahabah(صحابه), who came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said:

870
01:08:13,118 --> 01:08:17,266
The wealthy are doing this and this and this.

871
01:08:17,306 --> 01:08:21,031
They are giving out Sadaqah(صدقة), they are giving out Zaka'at(زكوة), they're fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

872
01:08:21,214 --> 01:08:23,555
they're supporting the fighters, while we're unable to do that.

873
01:08:23,610 --> 01:08:25,247
So Rasool Allah ﷺ told them to do what?

874
01:08:25,922 --> 01:08:27,033
He said: Go and make Zikr(زكر).

875
01:08:27,287 --> 01:08:29,101
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله), Allah o Akbar(الله أكبر).

876
01:08:29,549 --> 01:08:33,504
What happened is, the word got out to the wealthy, so they started doing the same thing.

877
01:08:34,844 --> 01:08:36,796
So the poor came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said,

878
01:08:37,217 --> 01:08:40,656
the secret that he gave us is now exposed, and the wealthy know about it.

879
01:08:40,955 --> 01:08:41,997
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

880
01:08:42,090 --> 01:08:43,541
ذَٰلِكَ فَضْلُ اللَّهِ يُؤْتِيهِ مَن يَشَاءُ ۚ

881
01:08:44,333 --> 01:08:46,698
This is a blessing from Allah that Allah gives, whomever He wants.

882
01:08:46,825 --> 01:08:48,817
I mean, it is something that Allah has already given them.

883
01:08:51,405 --> 01:08:56,205
So why not take advantage of what Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has already given to you.

884
01:08:56,696 --> 01:09:01,470
Now, I hope that I wouldn't be misunderstood here.

885
01:09:02,033 --> 01:09:05,177
Yani(يعني) Still, a west Muslim needs to be prepared and ready.

886
01:09:06,653 --> 01:09:12,940
But the thing is sometimes we want to do something.

887
01:09:13,896 --> 01:09:20,000
And just because we're attached to it emotionally, we don't look at the capabilities and skills,

888
01:09:20,254 --> 01:09:21,413
whether there are there or not.

889
01:09:23,937 --> 01:09:27,016
And especially when it comes to the area of Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

890
01:09:28,063 --> 01:09:30,230
these are difficulties that cannot be spoken out.

891
01:09:30,309 --> 01:09:33,617
These are difficulties that only could be understood when experienced.

892
01:09:34,754 --> 01:09:40,807
I mean, now when a person looks at it and they think about it intellectually, you know, it seems very easy,

893
01:09:41,381 --> 01:09:46,435
but you could be put in a situation that when your heart starts to pound and you feel it in your throat,

894
01:09:47,403 --> 01:09:50,753
and your eyes become dizzy and your body starts to sweat.

895
01:09:51,474 --> 01:09:55,139
Your mind can't really think clearly, the whole mind is clouded.

896
01:09:56,123 --> 01:10:00,065
So all of the ideas that you have and the Eeman(ايمان) that you have is under pressure at that moment.

897
01:10:00,718 --> 01:10:08,693
So a person could take a decision that they wouldn't naturally take when they are in a very relaxed environment like this.

898
01:10:09,592 --> 01:10:13,607
And this is something that happened with Sahabah رضي الله عنهم. Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

899
01:10:13,687 --> 01:10:20,338
إِذ جاءوكُم مِن فَوقِكُم وَمِن أَسفَلَ مِنكُم وَإِذ زاغَتِ الأَبصارُ وَبَلَغَتِ القُلوبُ الحَناجِرَ وَتَظُنّونَ بِاللَّهِ الظُّنونا۞

900
01:10:21,298 --> 01:10:25,382
They attack you from the top, from the bottom and your hearts were in your throats.

901
01:10:25,846 --> 01:10:31,863
The hearts were pounding so bad that they could feel it in their throat, and the eyes were all over the place.

902
01:10:32,440 --> 01:10:33,757
وَتَظُنّونَ بِاللَّهِ الظُّنونا

903
01:10:33,797 --> 01:10:36,283
And you started having doubts about Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

904
01:10:36,829 --> 01:10:39,853
هُنالِكَ ابتُلِيَ المُؤمِنونَ وَزُلزِلوا زِلزالًا شَديدًا۞

905
01:10:40,178 --> 01:10:42,849
That's when Allah tested the believers and they were shaken.

906
01:10:44,210 --> 01:10:52,983
So it's a very difficult thing so why would one want to forsake all of this Ajr(أجْر), were the doors of opportunity are open,

907
01:10:53,579 --> 01:10:56,602
and maybe put themselves in a situation that they wouldn't be able to handle.

908
01:10:57,030 --> 01:11:01,001
When you could receive the Ajr(أجْر) of Ghazoo(غزؤ) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عزَّوَجل), from the comfort of your home,

909
01:11:02,173 --> 01:11:03,796
the opportunity is there.

910
01:11:03,982 --> 01:11:07,506
Now if Jihad(جهاد) is farz Ain(فرض عين), it becomes farz Ain(فرض عين) with Al-Badn(ألبدن) and Al-Maal(ألمال).

911
01:11:09,482 --> 01:11:14,887
But there are some obstacles and difficulties placed on the way so sometimes it becomes impossible

912
01:11:15,377 --> 01:11:17,735
or very difficult to make Jihad(جهاد) Bil-Badn(بألبدن).

913
01:11:18,877 --> 01:11:24,454
But the Area of Jihad Bil Maal(جهادبالمال) is much easier, and is wide open and needs to be taken advantage of.

914
01:11:25,601 --> 01:11:31,125
If Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has opened for you this opportunity of having the Ajr(أجْر) of that Man who's climbing up the mountain,

915
01:11:31,228 --> 01:11:34,284
 under fire, and you're sitting in the comfort of your house.

916
01:11:35,290 --> 01:11:37,901
I mean, only an insane person would give up such an opportunity,

917
01:11:38,451 --> 01:11:43,062
because that man cannot dream of competing with you and Jihad Bil Maal(جهادبالمال), they cannot.

918
01:11:43,283 --> 01:11:44,429
That's the best that they could do.

919
01:11:45,252 --> 01:11:48,390
But you could now practice Jihad Bil Maal(جهادبالمال),

920
01:11:48,737 --> 01:11:53,522
and then eventually in the future, Allah will open up for you a way to make Jihad(جهاد) Bil-Badn(بألبدن).

921
01:11:53,867 --> 01:11:55,158
So you would have combined both.

922
01:11:56,204 --> 01:12:03,820
Now, why wait until all doors are closed, and then you would end up moving, maybe broke with Jihad(جهاد) Bil-Badn(بألبدن).

923
01:12:04,297 --> 01:12:04,597
Right!

924
01:12:05,242 --> 01:12:09,863
And, you would have missed out on so many opportunities to make Jihad Bil Maal(جهادبالمال).

925
01:12:10,975 --> 01:12:16,823
So the door of opportunities open the gates are wide open, one should not waste that opportunity.

926
01:12:16,902 --> 01:12:20,878
Now if we're going to go with the ruling of the Fuqahaa(فقهاء) that Jihad(جهاد) is mandatory once a year,

927
01:12:21,246 --> 01:12:27,826
then one would say that at least, I'm going to finance the family of Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) for an entire year,

928
01:12:28,141 --> 01:12:31,615
and you could do that promise Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ that you're going to do specific things

929
01:12:31,655 --> 01:12:35,092
you're going to sponsor specific causes, and go ahead with it.

930
01:12:35,871 --> 01:12:37,433
And there's so much that could be done

931
01:12:37,473 --> 01:12:44,566
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) as Muslims we are still tribal oriented and family oriented, especially in the eastern culture.

932
01:12:44,994 --> 01:12:47,079
Take advantage of the family and friend connections.

933
01:12:48,400 --> 01:12:49,274
Take advantage of that.

934
01:12:50,055 --> 01:12:57,916
You can network and you can take advantage of the family, relatives because Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله).

935
01:12:57,963 --> 01:13:03,393
Yani(يعني) still, our families, even if they would not agree with what we believe,

936
01:13:04,165 --> 01:13:07,150
it wouldn't go as far as betraying a family member.

937
01:13:08,002 --> 01:13:13,763
Yani(يعني) Rasool Allah ﷺ when he went to make the agreement of Al-Hijrah(ألهجرة) with Ansaar(ألأنْصَار).

938
01:13:14,239 --> 01:13:15,282
Who was he accompanying with.?

939
01:13:16,287 --> 01:13:18,605
He was accompanying with his uncle Al-Abbas(العباس), who wasn't a Muslim,

940
01:13:19,872 --> 01:13:25,568
but the family links are still there and his uncle would side with him even though he disagreed with that what Rasool Allah ﷺ was doing.

941
01:13:26,454 --> 01:13:32,364
And this still remains pretty much the norm, among our family especially in more tribalistic societies,

942
01:13:33,091 --> 01:13:37,841
that the links are there and they can be developed and taken advantage of.

943
01:13:38,657 --> 01:13:40,046
وضال على خير الكفاعلة

944
01:13:40,086 --> 01:13:45,318
The one who guides towards good will receive a copy of that Ajr(أجْر).

945
01:13:45,506 --> 01:13:50,526
ومن سن فيي الإسلام سنة حسنة كان له أجرها وأجر من عمل بها من بعده

946
01:13:51,127 --> 01:13:53,521
If you start to good Sunnah(سنة) in Islam

947
01:13:53,963 --> 01:13:58,847
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will give you the Ajr(أجْر) of that Sunnah(سنة) and Ajr(أجْر) of everyone who acts upon it.

948
01:13:59,019 --> 01:14:00,308
Back to the issue of Hijrah(هجرة).

949
01:14:00,646 --> 01:14:02,426
Let's be practical!

950
01:14:03,138 --> 01:14:06,448
What are you going to tell the people in the Muslims in the West to leave, just pack up and leave.

951
01:14:07,982 --> 01:14:08,836
Are they going to do that?

952
01:14:08,988 --> 01:14:13,560
Let's assume that we're going to tell everybody that's Haram(حرام) to stay here we have to pack up and leave.

953
01:14:14,934 --> 01:14:18,249
And if Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) from Makkah to Madina mandatory

954
01:14:18,342 --> 01:14:21,510
and there were still some Muslims who didn't move from Makkah.

955
01:14:21,999 --> 01:14:25,267
Do you expect that by telling Muslims in the West to make Hijrah(هجرة), they're gonna make Hijrah(هجرة).

956
01:14:26,320 --> 01:14:31,016
So you cannot control the wind, you cannot control the waves, but you can control your sail.

957
01:14:31,280 --> 01:14:34,654
So rather than telling the Muslims that is Farz Ain(فرض عين) on you to fight Jihad(جهاد).

958
01:14:34,694 --> 01:14:37,158
Now you have to move out and then they're gonna ask you, go where?

959
01:14:37,198 --> 01:14:41,319
And there's really nowhere to tell them, to go past the bucket around.

960
01:14:41,716 --> 01:14:43,045
Take advantage of what you can.

961
01:14:43,208 --> 01:14:45,847
Some things, it's gonna be impossible for you to change.

962
01:14:46,359 --> 01:14:50,286
Muslims love it in the West, and they were very reluctant to move out.

963
01:14:51,279 --> 01:14:53,247
So asking them to leave is impractical.

964
01:14:54,072 --> 01:15:01,310
But take advantage of the Muslims financial situation in the west, to support the cause of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

965
01:15:01,881 --> 01:15:07,915
And then what happens is, if Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ sees good in the hearts of these people,

966
01:15:08,416 --> 01:15:10,815
who supported His cause Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will find a way out for them.

967
01:15:11,656 --> 01:15:15,085
A very serious concern that brothers have is the issue of Ri'ya(رياء),

968
01:15:15,879 --> 01:15:18,119
when you read the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

969
01:15:20,212 --> 01:15:22,350
That the first to be thrown in Hellfire is the Shaheed(شَهِيد)

970
01:15:23,578 --> 01:15:28,469
that strikes fear in the hearts of many and it would make them hesitate,

971
01:15:30,159 --> 01:15:33,866
going out, because they would fear that they're not doing it for the right reasons,

972
01:15:34,770 --> 01:15:37,091
and sometimes Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) can use it to put fear in the heart,

973
01:15:37,535 --> 01:15:40,992
he tells you you're not really ready to die now because if you die you're not doing it for the sake of Allah.

974
01:15:41,334 --> 01:15:48,381
However, with the Jihad Bil Mal(جهادبالمال), the issue was much more clear and it's much more easier to have sincerity in it,

975
01:15:49,369 --> 01:15:53,986
because there's no fame and there's no bravado and there's no… Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) cannot play these games with you.

976
01:15:54,059 --> 01:15:56,925
Jihad Bil Mal(جهادبالمال) is something that can be done privately nobody knows about it.

977
01:15:57,758 --> 01:16:00,801
And this is how a person can develop a sincerity for the real thing.

978
01:16:01,300 --> 01:16:06,022
By continuously giving up that money and doing it in a sincere way privately,

979
01:16:06,284 --> 01:16:12,231
this would develop in the heart the sincerity for the cause so that you would go in with more confidence when the real thing starts.

980
01:16:12,517 --> 01:16:16,540
Plus, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will give you Toufeeq(توفيق), because of the way you started out.

981
01:16:16,873 --> 01:16:20,453
The punishment of withholding wealth from being spent in the path of Allah.

982
01:16:20,762 --> 01:16:21,958
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

983
01:16:22,190 --> 01:16:29,797
وَأَنفِقوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ وَلا تُلقوا بِأَيديكُم إِلَى التَّهلُكَةِ

984
01:16:30,349 --> 01:16:36,606
وَأَحسِنوا  إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ المُحسِنينَ۞

985
01:16:37,042 --> 01:16:38,757
And spend in the way of Allah.

986
01:16:38,899 --> 01:16:44,201
And do not throw yourselves with your own hands into destruction, and do good.

987
01:16:44,447 --> 01:16:46,769
Indeed, Allah loves the doers of good.

988
01:16:47,503 --> 01:16:54,045
وَأَنفِقوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ وَلا تُلقوا بِأَيديكُم إِلَى التَّهلُكَةِ  وَأَحسِنوا  إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ المُحسِنينَ۞

989
01:16:54,473 --> 01:17:01,594
Huzaifa(حذيفه) said: The meaning of this Ayah(آية) is that when people do not spend their wealth in the path of Allah,

990
01:17:02,047 --> 01:17:04,380
they are throwing themselves into destruction.

991
01:17:04,888 --> 01:17:05,788
And this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

992
01:17:06,233 --> 01:17:07,840
Ibn Abi Hatim(إبن أبي حاتم) in his Tafseer(تفسير),

993
01:17:08,298 --> 01:17:13,494
he says that this is the opinion of Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس), Iqrimah(عكرمة), Al-Hasan(ألحسن), Mujahid(مُجَاهِد), Ataa(عطاء),

994
01:17:13,677 --> 01:17:18,606
Saeed Ibn Jubair(سعيد إبن جبير), Salih Ad-Dahaat(صالح ألضاحات), As-Suddi(ألسدي), Qatil Ibn Hayyan(قاتل إبن حيَّان),

995
01:17:18,923 --> 01:17:20,242
Qatadah(قتادة) and others.

996
01:17:20,758 --> 01:17:27,533
So it's pretty much the accepted opinion that Tahluka(تهلكة) throwing yourself into destruction means not spending in the path of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

997
01:17:27,964 --> 01:17:34,691
Al-Qurtubi(قرطبي) states in his Tafseer(تفسير) that Hudhaifah(حذيفه), Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس), Ataa(عطاء), Iqrimah(عكرمة), Mujahid(مُجَاهِد) and others say

998
01:17:35,104 --> 01:17:39,777
that you shouldn't refrain from spending in the cause of Allah for fear of poverty.

999
01:17:40,625 --> 01:17:44,911
This is also the opinion of Bukhari(بخاريْ), and he didn't mention any other opinions.

1000
01:17:45,895 --> 01:17:46,674
Allah says:

1001
01:17:46,762 --> 01:18:02,065
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنوا إِنَّ كَثيرًا مِنَ الأَحبارِ وَالرُّهبانِ لَيَأكُلونَ أَموالَ النّاسِ بِالباطِلِ

1002
01:18:02,760 --> 01:18:11,683
لَيَأكُلونَ أَموالَ النّاسِ بِالباطِلِ وَيَصُدّونَ عَن سَبيلِ اللَّهِ ۗ

1003
01:18:12,045 --> 01:18:21,102
وَالَّذينَ يَكنِزونَ الذَّهَبَ وَالفِضَّةَ وَلا يُنفِقونَها في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ

1004
01:18:21,604 --> 01:18:30,191
وَلا يُنفِقونَها في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ فَبَشِّرهُم بِعَذابٍ أَليمٍ۞

1005
01:18:30,787 --> 01:18:41,853
يَومَ يُحمىٰ عَلَيها في نارِ جَهَنَّمَ فَتُكوىٰ بِها جِباهُهُم وَجُنوبُهُم وَظُهورُهُم ۖ

1006
01:18:42,702 --> 01:18:51,528
هٰذا ما كَنَزتُم لِأَنفُسِكُم فَذوقوا ما كُنتُم تَكنِزونَ۞

1007
01:18:51,644 --> 01:18:56,331
And those who hoard gold and silver, and spend it not in the way of Allah,

1008
01:18:56,776 --> 01:18:59,004
give them tidings of a painful punishment.

1009
01:18:59,784 --> 01:19:07,027
The day when it will be heated in the fire of hell and seared there with will be their foreheads, and flanks and backs.

1010
01:19:07,495 --> 01:19:10,735
That is what you hoarded for yourself, and taste what you used to hoard.

1011
01:19:11,243 --> 01:19:13,354
It's in At-Toba(التوبة) Verse 34, 35.

1012
01:19:13,751 --> 01:19:14,950
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

1013
01:19:15,545 --> 01:19:24,830
وَما لَكُم أَلّا تُنفِقوا في سَبيلِ اللَّهِ وَلِلَّهِ ميراثُ السَّماواتِ وَالأَرضِ ۚ

1014
01:19:25,691 --> 01:19:33,125
لا يَستَوي مِنكُم مَن أَنفَقَ مِن قَبلِ الفَتحِ وَقاتَلَ ۚ

1015
01:19:33,697 --> 01:19:43,253
أُولٰئِكَ أَعظَمُ دَرَجَةً مِنَ الَّذينَ أَنفَقوا مِن بَعدُ وَقاتَلوا ۚ

1016
01:19:43,949 --> 01:19:48,150
وَكُلًّا وَعَدَ اللَّهُ الحُسنىٰ ۚ

1017
01:19:48,520 --> 01:19:53,557
وَاللَّهُ بِما تَعمَلونَ خَبيرٌ۞

1018
01:19:54,411 --> 01:19:59,822
And why do you not spend in the cause of Allah, while to Allah belongs the heritage of the heavens on Earth.

1019
01:20:00,029 --> 01:20:01,037
Al-Hadid(ألحديد) verse 10.

1020
01:20:01,822 --> 01:20:04,084
Aslam Abi Amran(أسلم أبي عمران) said:

1021
01:20:04,354 --> 01:20:08,963
We were in a army heading from Madina towards Constantinople,

1022
01:20:09,923 --> 01:20:12,630
the head of the army was Abdul Rahman Ibn Khalid Ibn Walid(عبدالرحمن إبن خالد إبن وليد),

1023
01:20:13,074 --> 01:20:15,965
Romans had their backs facing the gates of the city.

1024
01:20:16,879 --> 01:20:20,465
So a man from among us, rushed alone, towards the enemy.

1025
01:20:21,585 --> 01:20:25,756
Some people said there is no god but Allah, he is throwing himself into destruction.

1026
01:20:26,287 --> 01:20:29,328
So here you have the two armies did not fight yet.

1027
01:20:29,939 --> 01:20:38,198
So the rank does not mix, and you have this Muslim soldier, he just shoots out straight and attacks the Roman.

1028
01:20:38,325 --> 01:20:39,905
So some soldiers who saw that they said:

1029
01:20:39,945 --> 01:20:41,176
تُلقوا بِأَيديه إِلَى التَّهلُكَةِ

1030
01:20:41,255 --> 01:20:44,009
He is throwing himself into destruction and they quoting this Ayah(آية).

1031
01:20:44,374 --> 01:20:50,166
Abu Ayub Al-Ansari(أبوأيوب ألأنصاري) who heard that, he said, this verse was revealed, speaking about us the Ansaar(أنصار).

1032
01:20:50,372 --> 01:20:53,778
When Allah gave His Messenger victory and Islam prevailed.

1033
01:20:54,023 --> 01:20:57,189
We said: Let's go back to our businesses and take care of it.

1034
01:20:57,364 --> 01:21:01,563
The Ansaar(أنصار) made an agreement with Rasool Allah ﷺ, to give him victory,

1035
01:21:01,876 --> 01:21:04,037
and in exchange they will be given Jannah(جنة).

1036
01:21:04,169 --> 01:21:06,598
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gave Muhammad(محمد) victory when he opened Makkah,

1037
01:21:06,653 --> 01:21:08,814
so Khalas(خلاص), Ansaar(أنصار) said:

1038
01:21:08,886 --> 01:21:10,402
We'll go back to our farms now,

1039
01:21:10,751 --> 01:21:14,576
take care of our businesses, Allah has given Muhammadﷺ victory, he opens his hometown,

1040
01:21:14,933 --> 01:21:19,925
it's over with our businesses suffered, our farms were not taking care of.

1041
01:21:20,401 --> 01:21:23,846
It's about time for us to go and take care of business.

1042
01:21:24,385 --> 01:21:26,530
And that's when Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed this Ayah(آية),

1043
01:21:26,696 --> 01:21:28,561
وَلا تُلقوا بِأَيديكُم إِلَى التَّهلُكَةِ

1044
01:21:28,784 --> 01:21:32,967
That you are throwing yourselves into destruction, you're not spending in the path of Allah.

1045
01:21:33,331 --> 01:21:39,297
So, withholding the Nafaqa(نفقة), from the Path of Allah, destroying themselves into destruction.

1046
01:21:39,467 --> 01:21:40,395
Abu Ayub(أبوأيوب) says:

1047
01:21:40,474 --> 01:21:45,829
So throwing ourselves into destruction, meant going back to our farms and businesses and leaving Jihad(جهاد).

1048
01:21:46,924 --> 01:21:47,956
Abu Amran(أبوعمران) said:

1049
01:21:48,178 --> 01:21:51,924
Abu Ayub(أبوأيوب) remained in Jihad(جهاد) until he was buried in Constantinople.

1050
01:21:52,337 --> 01:21:55,660
This is in Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ) and Al-Hakim(ألحاكم).

1051
01:21:56,557 --> 01:22:02,269
Al-Qasim Bin Makhrama(ألقاسم بن مخرمة), one of Tabieen(تابعين) and he said:

1052
01:22:03,567 --> 01:22:10,968
Destruction is withholding, spending in the cause of Allah, but if a man alone attacks 10,000 strong of the enemy that is fine.

1053
01:22:11,048 --> 01:22:11,905
And Allah knows best.

1054
01:22:12,484 --> 01:22:15,262
And this is in Sunan Al-Kubra(سنن ألكبرى), in At-Tabari(ألطبري) in his Tafseer(تفسير).

1055
01:22:15,913 --> 01:22:22,357
The author says Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) may tell you that since you might die, Why not leave your wealth behind for your family!

1056
01:22:22,865 --> 01:22:26,219
This thought is only accepted by one was little trust on Allah.

1057
01:22:26,952 --> 01:22:30,163
It shows the existence of doubts in Allah's ability to provide,

1058
01:22:30,560 --> 01:22:35,767
because if you believe that you are nothing but the middleman between Allah and your family,

1059
01:22:36,164 --> 01:22:42,918
and that's in realities is not you who is providing for them, then you would not worry for your family after you die.

1060
01:22:44,045 --> 01:22:49,305
Abu Dhar(ابوزر) said that the Messenger of Allah saw me entering, and they were sitting under the Shade of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

1061
01:22:49,964 --> 01:22:54,712
When he saw me, he said, In the name of the Lord of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), they are the great losers.

1062
01:22:55,495 --> 01:22:59,409
I couldn't help but go to him and ask, who they were, he said:

1063
01:22:59,520 --> 01:23:05,211
The wealthy, except for those who spend it like this and he waved his hand, left right behind.

1064
01:23:05,433 --> 01:23:07,353
And then he said: And few are they.

1065
01:23:07,711 --> 01:23:09,293
This is in Muslim(ألمسلم) and Bukhari(بخاريْ).

1066
01:23:12,915 --> 01:23:20,638
Next session section, the virtues of providing for the fighters in Allah’s path, and taking care of their families.

1067
01:23:23,262 --> 01:23:27,129
Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(أبوسعيد ألخدري) said that the messenger of Allah sent an army to Banu Lahyan(بنولحيان).

1068
01:23:27,945 --> 01:23:30,582
He said: From every two men one goes out.

1069
01:23:31,217 --> 01:23:33,425
Then he told the one staying behind.

1070
01:23:34,305 --> 01:23:43,013
Whoever of you takes care of his brother's family, until he comes back would receive half the reward of those who went out.

1071
01:23:43,677 --> 01:23:46,098
Now the next Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

1072
01:23:46,250 --> 01:23:49,742
Whoever provides for a fighter in the cause of Allah has actually fought,

1073
01:23:50,276 --> 01:23:53,501
and whoever takes care of the family of a fighter has actually fought.

1074
01:23:54,485 --> 01:23:56,838
How do you combine between the two Hadith(حديث).

1075
01:23:57,659 --> 01:24:02,528
One Hadith(حديث), it says if you support the fighter, you have fought,

1076
01:24:03,516 --> 01:24:05,587
the other Hadith(حديث) says you receive half the Ajr(أجْر),

1077
01:24:06,330 --> 01:24:07,441
How do you combined between the two?

1078
01:24:07,635 --> 01:24:10,128
The second Hadith(حديث) apparently means that you receive the same Ajr(أجْر).

1079
01:24:10,532 --> 01:24:12,073
من جهز غازي فقد غزة

1080
01:24:12,711 --> 01:24:14,551
The one who supports a fighter has fought,

1081
01:24:15,467 --> 01:24:20,706
the Hadith(حديث) before says, if you support the fighter, he will get half the Ajr(أجْر) and you get half.

1082
01:24:21,506 --> 01:24:22,595
So, what does that mean.?

1083
01:24:22,927 --> 01:24:26,331
Well the answer is not definitive anyway but it's an opinion of one of the scholars,

1084
01:24:27,151 --> 01:24:34,533
that if a person supports a fighter the Ajr(أجْر) is split between two,

1085
01:24:34,813 --> 01:24:36,560
so they receive the same Ajr(أجْر).

1086
01:24:36,768 --> 01:24:42,968
However, if a person goes out and they support themselves, they will be receiving double the Ajr(أجْر), so it's clear.

1087
01:24:43,098 --> 01:24:46,308
So, there's a difference between somebody who goes out and finances himself,

1088
01:24:46,467 --> 01:24:48,005
and somebody who was financed by other.

1089
01:24:48,731 --> 01:24:53,519
If a person is financed by others they receive half the Ajr(أجْر) the other half goes to the one, who finances.

1090
01:24:54,142 --> 01:24:56,581
But if a person goes out and they finance themselves.

1091
01:24:56,747 --> 01:24:57,662
It is double the Ajr(أجْر).

1092
01:24:58,277 --> 01:24:58,746
So the Hadith(حديث),

1093
01:24:58,786 --> 01:24:59,796
من جهز غازي فقد غزة

1094
01:25:00,788 --> 01:25:04,410
Means you receive the Ajr(أجْر) of somebody, who went out but didn't finance themselves.

1095
01:25:04,547 --> 01:25:06,026
So the Ajr(أجْر) is split between two.

1096
01:25:07,447 --> 01:25:08,436
Ibn Masood(إبن مسعود) said:

1097
01:25:09,143 --> 01:25:14,053
For me to equip a fighter with a whip is better to me than making Hajj(حَجْ).

1098
01:25:14,190 --> 01:25:17,162
This is narrated by Ibn Mubarak(إبن مبارك) and Ibn Abi Shaibah(إبن أبي شعيبة).

1099
01:25:17,305 --> 01:25:22,570
Odae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم) asked, the Messenger of Allah, about the best Sadaqah(صدقة), the Messenger of Allah said:

1100
01:25:23,330 --> 01:25:26,317
Serving your companions in the path of Allah, he said and then what?

1101
01:25:26,645 --> 01:25:30,850
The messenger of Allah said: Building a structure that would provide them with Shade.

1102
01:25:31,458 --> 01:25:33,114
He said: And then what the messenger of Allah said:

1103
01:25:33,164 --> 01:25:35,794
A saddle for a horse in the path of Allah,

1104
01:25:35,956 --> 01:25:38,060
and this Sunan Saeed Ibn Mansoor(سنن سعيد بن منصور).

1105
01:25:38,554 --> 01:25:43,922
Amir Bin Qais(عامر بن قيس), he is one of the Tabieen(تابعين), he used to participate in Jihad(جهاد) against the Romans.

1106
01:25:44,584 --> 01:25:47,503
He had the mule, which he would share with a Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين).

1107
01:25:48,585 --> 01:25:54,201
When he was about to join an army, he would go around, glancing at the faces of people and studying them.

1108
01:25:55,220 --> 01:25:57,788
If he sees a group of men who would suit him.

1109
01:25:58,159 --> 01:26:02,811
He would walk up to them and say, I would like to join you but I have three conditions.

1110
01:26:03,283 --> 01:26:08,129
So now this is one of the Tabieen(تابعين), who was going out in an army.

1111
01:26:08,594 --> 01:26:10,842
He wants to make sure that he has the right company with him,

1112
01:26:10,885 --> 01:26:12,157
you know the Army is large,

1113
01:26:12,681 --> 01:26:16,508
but there's going to be an exclusive group that you're going to be with, most of the time, in the same tent,

1114
01:26:16,580 --> 01:26:22,087
it's your small group that you cling to, so he want to make sure that he is with the right people,

1115
01:26:22,358 --> 01:26:29,621
you know, when the rain start, raining as they say, you want to make sure that you have good brothers on your sides.

1116
01:26:29,959 --> 01:26:33,512
 Just like Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) in the battle of Badr(بدر), he said:

1117
01:26:33,761 --> 01:26:37,327
When I was in the rank, two young boys came next to me.

1118
01:26:38,114 --> 01:26:44,072
And I wished that Allah would send me somebody older to give me strength in the battle,

1119
01:26:44,152 --> 01:26:46,372
you know, he have these two kids next to him, it doesn't feel right.

1120
01:26:47,721 --> 01:26:52,197
So Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) wasn't really happy that these are the two, who are flanking him in the rank.

1121
01:26:52,660 --> 01:26:55,501
And while he was asking for something better.

1122
01:26:56,512 --> 01:26:59,680
The one on his right, poked him and said:

1123
01:26:59,766 --> 01:27:02,899
O uncle! Tell me, where is Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)?

1124
01:27:03,170 --> 01:27:04,913
Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: What do you want about Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)?

1125
01:27:04,953 --> 01:27:05,924
Yani(يعني) who are you?

1126
01:27:06,401 --> 01:27:07,655
He said: What do you want from Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)?

1127
01:27:08,621 --> 01:27:14,897
He said: I heard and these were Ansaar(أنصار). He said: I heard that Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), was the worst enemy of Rasool Ullah,

1128
01:27:15,406 --> 01:27:19,751
so I don't want my body to leave his, until one of us kills the other.

1129
01:27:20,359 --> 01:27:21,273
So I told him,

1130
01:27:22,067 --> 01:27:27,329
and he said: Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: And then the one on my left, poked me, and he said: O uncle, where's Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).?

1131
01:27:28,705 --> 01:27:30,431
So I told them: Do you see that man?

1132
01:27:30,570 --> 01:27:36,526
And Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) says that he was like, you could know him because of the people surrounding him, very crowded.

1133
01:27:36,606 --> 01:27:37,974
He said: Do you see that man over there?

1134
01:27:38,305 --> 01:27:38,972
That's Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

1135
01:27:40,785 --> 01:27:48,269
So Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن) said: They shot off like Falcons from both sides, and attacked Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل),

1136
01:27:48,597 --> 01:27:54,061
so you know don't estimate the person by the size or by the looks, you never know what hidden insight, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله).

1137
01:27:54,758 --> 01:27:57,567
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) was asking for something better, he did not know,

1138
01:27:58,030 --> 01:28:00,966
that he was flanked by the two men who will actually kill Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

1139
01:28:01,184 --> 01:28:05,946
They're the ones, who disabled him, but then it was Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) who finished him of.

1140
01:28:06,283 --> 01:28:10,157
So what were the conditions that Amir Bin Qais(عامر بن قيس) make on his group?

1141
01:28:10,237 --> 01:28:12,003
Look at these conditions, three conditions.

1142
01:28:12,425 --> 01:28:17,797
He said, that I become your servant and I don't want anybody competing with me.

1143
01:28:18,372 --> 01:28:24,062
My condition is that you allow me to be the servant and nobody else competes with me in serving.

1144
01:28:24,478 --> 01:28:30,346
Number two, I become the one who calls the Adhan(آذَان) among you and I don't want anybody to compete with me in that.

1145
01:28:31,530 --> 01:28:34,931
Number three, I cover your expenses according to my ability.

1146
01:28:36,884 --> 01:28:38,288
If they agree, he would join them.

1147
01:28:38,715 --> 01:28:42,714
If they ever compete with them he would depart them and move on to find another group.

1148
01:28:44,325 --> 01:28:45,887
So he was quite serious about it.

1149
01:28:46,564 --> 01:28:47,828
And this is in Ibn Ul-Mubarak(إبن المبارك).

1150
01:28:48,921 --> 01:28:49,952
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

1151
01:28:50,471 --> 01:28:57,066
The early Muslims, if they would go out in armies they would strive to serve others and to make their company happy,

1152
01:28:57,670 --> 01:29:03,306
they would prefer others to themselves, they will do all of that for the sake of Allah and to gain His pleasure.

1153
01:29:03,800 --> 01:29:13,730
The issue of service, especially among the Mujahideen(مجاهدين), is an extremely important psychological thing for the group,

1154
01:29:14,231 --> 01:29:18,456
because it gives a whole different flavor to the entire environment,

1155
01:29:19,073 --> 01:29:22,569
and it closes the door on Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) because Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

1156
01:29:23,077 --> 01:29:26,448
وقل لعبادي يقولوا التي هي أحسن إن الشيطان ينزغ بينهم

1157
01:29:26,943 --> 01:29:32,396
Tell My servants to speak good words because Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) wants to cause you disunity among them.

1158
01:29:33,385 --> 01:29:39,640
And what happens is, in that environment Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) tries to take advantage of the difficulty of the environment

1159
01:29:39,695 --> 01:29:45,582
because see when everything is getting on your nerves, you tend to be a bit intolerant,

1160
01:29:45,677 --> 01:29:48,681
and hot tempered, and that happens in travel.

1161
01:29:49,188 --> 01:29:50,915
It happens when you change your diet.

1162
01:29:51,557 --> 01:29:53,456
It happens when the climate changes.

1163
01:29:53,905 --> 01:29:57,849
So, all of this gets to you, and you lose your temper.

1164
01:29:58,471 --> 01:30:03,483
And that's why when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) heard somebody praising another Muslim.

1165
01:30:04,183 --> 01:30:05,833
He said: Did you do business with him?

1166
01:30:05,868 --> 01:30:06,402
He said: No!

1167
01:30:06,482 --> 01:30:07,440
He said: Did you travel with him?

1168
01:30:07,480 --> 01:30:08,001
He said: No!

1169
01:30:08,041 --> 01:30:09,600
He said: Then how can you make a judgment on that person?

1170
01:30:10,968 --> 01:30:13,813
So, there are some issues that bring the truth out of a person.

1171
01:30:13,853 --> 01:30:19,081
Because we put up sometimes some public manners.

1172
01:30:20,224 --> 01:30:20,565
Right!

1173
01:30:20,895 --> 01:30:24,344
But if you want to dig deep into this real person.

1174
01:30:24,778 --> 01:30:28,353
You have to put them through a test, Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

1175
01:30:30,258 --> 01:30:35,721
So, in the environment of Jihad(جهاد) because of all of these restraints and difficulties,

1176
01:30:36,284 --> 01:30:41,170
the issue of service becomes very important because it is, what develops the love among the group,

1177
01:30:41,656 --> 01:30:46,789
you know when your brother, who could be older than you more experienced than you, wealthier than you,

1178
01:30:48,056 --> 01:30:51,723
he comes and he serves you and he helps you out and he brings you the food,

1179
01:30:52,853 --> 01:30:58,137
that is something that you would never forget, and this is what develops the love among the brothers,

1180
01:30:58,673 --> 01:31:03,753
so the issue of Khidma(خدمة), the issue of service is an extremely important area.

1181
01:31:04,543 --> 01:31:08,713
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) when it comes to Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), there must be love among the group

1182
01:31:08,872 --> 01:31:13,569
because you live and die with these people, that Muhabbah(محبة) has to be there.

1183
01:31:14,241 --> 01:31:17,717
It's not good to die when you have some bad feelings against the person, next to you.

1184
01:31:19,110 --> 01:31:23,585
Tayeb(طيِّب), Next chapter is chapter four, the virtues of Ribat(رباط).

1185
01:31:26,759 --> 01:31:30,073
And the virtues of the one, who dies in Ribat(رباط).

1186
01:31:30,959 --> 01:31:32,687
We talked about the definition of Ribat(رباط).

1187
01:31:33,310 --> 01:31:34,219
Did we talk about Ribat(رباط)?

1188
01:31:34,543 --> 01:31:36,563
We did, I think. So the meaning is clear,

1189
01:31:36,929 --> 01:31:37,808
Allah says:

1190
01:31:38,064 --> 01:31:45,879
فَإِذَا انسَلَخَ الأَشهُرُ الحُرُمُ فَاقتُلُوا المُشرِكينَ حَيثُ وَجَدتُموهُم

1191
01:31:46,182 --> 01:31:51,742
وَخُذوهُم وَاحصُروهُم وَاقعُدوا لَهُم كُلَّ مَرصَدٍ ۚ

1192
01:31:52,080 --> 01:31:59,975
فَإِن تابوا وَأَقامُوا الصَّلاةَ وَآتَوُا الزَّكاةَ فَخَلّوا سَبيلَهُم ۚ

1193
01:32:00,288 --> 01:32:04,285
إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفورٌ رَحيمٌ۞

1194
01:32:04,600 --> 01:32:09,797
Then kill the ones who are associated with Allah, other gods, wherever you find them,

1195
01:32:10,236 --> 01:32:16,351
and capture them, and the besiege them and sit and wait for them at every place of ambush,

1196
01:32:17,190 --> 01:32:19,051
And this is Surah At-Toba(سورةالتوبة) verse 5.

1197
01:32:19,540 --> 01:32:21,319
وَاقعُدوا لَهُم كُلَّ مَرصَدٍ

1198
01:32:21,493 --> 01:32:27,691
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر), he says that, this Ayah(آية) means that you not only target the Kuffar(كفار).

1199
01:32:28,108 --> 01:32:32,927
But you wait for them, and you ambush them, and you try to get to them.

1200
01:32:33,910 --> 01:32:35,760
And this is Ribat(رباط) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1201
01:32:36,901 --> 01:32:40,504
So it's not just you fight them when you see them, you go after them

1202
01:32:40,544 --> 01:32:42,094
and Allah says,

1203
01:32:42,248 --> 01:32:43,365
وَاقعُدوا لَهُم كُلَّ مَرصَدٍ

1204
01:32:43,646 --> 01:32:48,668
Ambush, and that need Sabr(صبر), and that's Ribat(رباط) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says:

1205
01:32:48,763 --> 01:32:56,112
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنُوا اصبِروا وَصابِروا وَرابِطوا

1206
01:32:56,472 --> 01:33:02,394
وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُم تُفلِحونَ۞

1207
01:33:03,418 --> 01:33:07,636
O you have believed, persevere and endure and remain stationed.

1208
01:33:08,039 --> 01:33:12,637
 And fear Allah that you may be successful and this is Al-Imran(ألعمران) verse 200 .

1209
01:33:12,795 --> 01:33:19,425
يا أَيُّهَا الَّذينَ آمَنُوا اصبِروا وَصابِروا وَرابِطوا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُم تُفلِحونَ۞

1210
01:33:19,465 --> 01:33:21,278
This is the last Ayah(آية) in Surat Al-Imran(سورة ألعمران).

1211
01:33:22,022 --> 01:33:26,987
The Ayah(آية) starts by calling the believers to have Sabr(صبر), patience.

1212
01:33:27,403 --> 01:33:30,163
Now what if your enemies also patient.

1213
01:33:31,066 --> 01:33:31,732
What do you do then?

1214
01:33:32,617 --> 01:33:34,185
You could be patient and then your enemy is patient.

1215
01:33:34,674 --> 01:33:36,064
And that's why it says:

1216
01:33:36,104 --> 01:33:36,736
وَصابِروا

1217
01:33:37,383 --> 01:33:38,881
Saabiroo(صابرو) is Seegha Al-Mufaila(صيغة ألمفاعلة)

1218
01:33:39,312 --> 01:33:41,644
which is something that happens between two sides.

1219
01:33:42,628 --> 01:33:46,414
Sabr(صبر) is something that you do on your own. That doesn't really relate to anybody else.

1220
01:33:47,521 --> 01:33:53,995
But Mufa'ala(مفاعلة) is something that is between two sides.

1221
01:33:54,329 --> 01:33:59,125
Saabiroo(صابرو) means and this is what the Mufasireen(مفسرين) and early scholars say,

1222
01:33:59,960 --> 01:34:04,312
it means that you outdo the enemy in his patience.

1223
01:34:05,661 --> 01:34:11,648
So you could be patient, the enemy could be patient, but you need to have Musabira(مصابرة), so you outdo them in your patience.

1224
01:34:11,728 --> 01:34:14,641
So you're competing with them, and who can endure more.

1225
01:34:15,634 --> 01:34:19,204
And this is a very important concept in war, who would break first.

1226
01:34:20,596 --> 01:34:24,130
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) in Gazwat Ul Yarmook(غزوة اليرموك), what he did.!

1227
01:34:24,820 --> 01:34:30,660
The Muslims were a little over I think 30,000, while the enemy was 200,000, plus.

1228
01:34:30,882 --> 01:34:32,756
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) wanted to lay siege to this army.

1229
01:34:32,903 --> 01:34:37,677
Now, how could 30,000 besiege 200,000.?

1230
01:34:38,649 --> 01:34:40,231
So what Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) did!

1231
01:34:40,578 --> 01:34:44,824
And he had, Yani(يعني) his flanks, do that for him, primarily, Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص),

1232
01:34:45,404 --> 01:34:46,039
He said:

1233
01:34:46,997 --> 01:34:49,306
Surround them and have their backs,

1234
01:34:49,346 --> 01:34:50,281
see because,

1235
01:34:50,540 --> 01:34:51,915
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), what the Romans did,

1236
01:34:52,013 --> 01:35:00,207
and this shows you how sometimes you try to protect yourself from something and your protection ends up being your demise.

1237
01:35:01,855 --> 01:35:03,568
The Romans had already had.

1238
01:35:04,019 --> 01:35:06,658
They already had experience with fighting the Muslims.

1239
01:35:07,269 --> 01:35:10,695
And what happened was they would always run away.

1240
01:35:10,735 --> 01:35:13,076
The soldiers didn't have the will to fight, so they would run away.

1241
01:35:13,754 --> 01:35:14,651
So what the Romans did?

1242
01:35:15,341 --> 01:35:16,934
Heracul(هراقل) actually, Heracules?

1243
01:35:17,935 --> 01:35:25,704
He ordered his brother who was the leader of the army to place the army in a place where there is no way they can run away.

1244
01:35:26,310 --> 01:35:27,561
And the only option is to fight.

1245
01:35:28,715 --> 01:35:32,887
So what Theodore did was, he chose the valley of Yarmook(يرموك).

1246
01:35:33,509 --> 01:35:38,256
This is the cliff to be towards their back, so they had a cliff towards their back

1247
01:35:40,844 --> 01:35:45,918
and they tied the soldiers in chains so every 10 soldiers are tied together in chains.

1248
01:35:46,537 --> 01:35:49,053
When Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) saw that even before the battle, he said:

1249
01:35:49,504 --> 01:35:51,873
أبشِرو فقيما يعتي بمحصورٌ بخير

1250
01:35:52,507 --> 01:35:57,245
Rejoice because rarely does a person who corners himself, ever come up with any good,

1251
01:35:57,636 --> 01:36:00,087
they tie themselves up in chains and they have their backs towards the cliff.

1252
01:36:02,250 --> 01:36:06,110
So what Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said is, just surround them from three sides and let the cliff behind.

1253
01:36:07,343 --> 01:36:08,493
So that's what the Muslims did.

1254
01:36:10,213 --> 01:36:14,218
But in order to be able to cluster them together and besiege them,

1255
01:36:14,902 --> 01:36:18,388
because the army was huge and the Muslims are only 30,000.

1256
01:36:19,040 --> 01:36:24,985
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) had to keep on cracking the army, again and again with the Al-Qarr Wal Farr(ألكرَّوالفرَّ).

1257
01:36:25,879 --> 01:36:29,014
Yani(يعني) you strike and you retreat, you strike and you retreat.

1258
01:36:30,155 --> 01:36:37,776
And one of those strikes Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), and about Allah O Alam(ألله أعلم), a few 100 horsemen with him.

1259
01:36:39,064 --> 01:36:41,672
It was the horsemen who do the brunt of this Al-Qarr Wal Farr(ألكرَّوالفرَّ).

1260
01:36:42,466 --> 01:36:47,120
They hit the army, so strong, and in that strike about 4000 died.

1261
01:36:47,628 --> 01:36:48,764
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said:

1262
01:36:49,374 --> 01:36:51,456
When they, when they came out, he said:

1263
01:36:51,804 --> 01:36:54,880
We have pushed them to the limits, if you hit them again they're gonna break.

1264
01:36:55,992 --> 01:36:58,489
He said: And Allah O Alam(ألله أعلم), how Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) knew that

1265
01:36:58,529 --> 01:37:03,285
maybe he looked in their eyes or their actions, but he said we have hit them to the limit.

1266
01:37:03,749 --> 01:37:05,169
If you hit them again they're gonna break.

1267
01:37:06,449 --> 01:37:08,722
 And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), that was the case.

1268
01:37:09,691 --> 01:37:11,754
So what he did is he was able to surround them.

1269
01:37:12,730 --> 01:37:17,975
And then he told part of his army to drive a wedge between the infantry, and the cavalry,

1270
01:37:19,148 --> 01:37:20,890
to drive a wedge between them and separate the two,

1271
01:37:21,415 --> 01:37:23,875
because the infantry depends on the cavalry for cover.

1272
01:37:24,168 --> 01:37:25,445
They drove a wedge between the two.

1273
01:37:25,695 --> 01:37:30,401
And then Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said, to Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), who was surrounding the cavalry,

1274
01:37:30,670 --> 01:37:33,981
he said: Open for them and exit gate, open for them an exit.

1275
01:37:34,618 --> 01:37:36,868
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) knew that if you open it up, they're gonna run out.

1276
01:37:38,030 --> 01:37:43,364
So the exit was opened, the cavalry ran out, and that is one Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) just besieged the infantry.

1277
01:37:43,739 --> 01:37:46,618
And what they did is they just push them from that cliff.

1278
01:37:47,129 --> 01:37:50,997
They say that about 80,000 fell and died.

1279
01:37:51,549 --> 01:37:52,718
Because what happens is they said:

1280
01:37:53,426 --> 01:37:59,763
If you would kill one or two soldiers from the 10 and push them, they will drag all of the rest with them.

1281
01:38:00,630 --> 01:38:03,765
So it was a disaster for the Romans Theodore was killed.

1282
01:38:03,913 --> 01:38:06,961
About half of the Roman army was wiped out.

1283
01:38:07,489 --> 01:38:10,550
And it was one of the greatest victories for the Muslims, Ghazwa Tul-Yarmook(غزوة اليرموك).

1284
01:38:11,230 --> 01:38:16,479
So this is the reason why I brought this up is the issue of Masabara(مصابرة).

1285
01:38:16,858 --> 01:38:17,986
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said:

1286
01:38:18,298 --> 01:38:21,960
 We have pushed them to the limit, strike them again, and they're going to crack.

1287
01:38:24,834 --> 01:38:33,616
The story of Antara Bin Shaddad(أنتراع بن شداد), Antara(أنتراع) is a legendary figure in non Islamic Arabia, it was before Islam

1288
01:38:34,364 --> 01:38:37,170
and Antara(أنتراع) was like Robin Hood in the English literature.

1289
01:38:38,647 --> 01:38:40,678
He is undefeated warrior.

1290
01:38:42,990 --> 01:38:44,185
So a man came to Antara(أنتراع).

1291
01:38:44,225 --> 01:38:47,454
This was a powerful man, he came, he came to Antara(أنتراع), he said:

1292
01:38:47,494 --> 01:38:49,812
How come you always win against your opponents.

1293
01:38:50,304 --> 01:38:50,945
What's the secret?

1294
01:38:51,234 --> 01:38:51,948
Antara(أنتراع) said:

1295
01:38:51,999 --> 01:38:57,038
Stick your finger in my mouth and I'll stick my finger in yours, and let's both bite.

1296
01:38:57,223 --> 01:38:59,511
So every one of them is biting on the finger of the other,

1297
01:38:59,760 --> 01:39:02,119
and then they're just squeezing cracking the bone.

1298
01:39:02,396 --> 01:39:04,616
So this guy, he screamed.

1299
01:39:06,502 --> 01:39:08,685
Antara(أنتراع) said that's why I win against my opponents.

1300
01:39:09,042 --> 01:39:09,768
He said: What do you mean?

1301
01:39:10,278 --> 01:39:15,183
He said: If you would have just waited for one more moment, I would have screamed, myself.

1302
01:39:16,183 --> 01:39:22,334
And that's how come I win, it is because I am willing to wait for that additional moment,

1303
01:39:22,685 --> 01:39:24,995
I'm willing to endure, one more moment.

1304
01:39:26,293 --> 01:39:30,619
So that's what it is, it is Musabra(مصابرة), you just wait, push it a little bit further,

1305
01:39:31,044 --> 01:39:32,463
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will give you the Nasr(نصر).

1306
01:39:32,996 --> 01:39:33,665
ورابطو

1307
01:39:34,260 --> 01:39:35,222
Remains stationed.

1308
01:39:36,006 --> 01:39:36,830
Al Hasan(ألحسن) said:

1309
01:39:36,927 --> 01:39:42,615
The meaning of persevere and endure in the verse is that the Muslims were commanded to outdo the non believers

1310
01:39:43,085 --> 01:39:49,018
in endurance and steadfastness until the non believers, end up giving up their religion.

1311
01:39:50,974 --> 01:39:52,709
Ibn Jarir(إبن جرير), he says:

1312
01:39:52,753 --> 01:39:55,864
Muhammad Ibn Ka'ab Al-Quradhi(محمد إبن كعب ألقرظي) used to say about this verse.

1313
01:39:56,584 --> 01:40:04,420
Be stationed in the Cause of Allah, until the nonbeliever leaves his religion for yours.

1314
01:40:05,408 --> 01:40:08,829
So the Musabra(مصابرة) here according to Muhammad Ibn Ka'ab Al-Quradhi(محمد إبن كعب ألقرظي)

1315
01:40:10,303 --> 01:40:18,779
is that you keep on putting pressure until this man gives up his religion and says, Alright, fine, I'll take yours.

1316
01:40:20,036 --> 01:40:23,142
And that is Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) exactly what happened between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

1317
01:40:23,579 --> 01:40:28,190
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were putting up a fight, Badr(بدر), Uhud(أحَد), Khandaq(خندق), Al-Hudaybiyah(ألحديبية).

1318
01:40:28,927 --> 01:40:29,828
In the end what happened!

1319
01:40:29,976 --> 01:40:35,834
Started hearing statements like, what have these gods done for us, or like another statement,

1320
01:40:36,129 --> 01:40:39,625
هذه قط سيوف قبح الله ما أغنيت عنى شيئَا

1321
01:40:40,033 --> 01:40:42,550
These swords are useless they haven't done us any good.

1322
01:40:43,027 --> 01:40:46,676
So they were giving up, they were losing hope in their gods.

1323
01:40:47,222 --> 01:40:49,074
Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), he said, these gods are worthless.

1324
01:40:51,094 --> 01:40:56,663
So they gave up their pagan worshipping, and they came into the fold of Islam.

1325
01:40:56,981 --> 01:40:57,450
How come?

1326
01:40:57,490 --> 01:40:59,257
Because of the Murabadha(مرابضى) and Musabra(مصابرة).

1327
01:41:06,892 --> 01:41:12,301
Messenger of Allah said: Being stationed for a day in the cause of Allah is better than the world and everything on it.

1328
01:41:12,556 --> 01:41:13,423
This is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

1329
01:41:14,704 --> 01:41:17,503
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said, the Messenger of Allah said:

1330
01:41:18,155 --> 01:41:24,730
Being stationed in the path of Allah for a day is greater than fasting the days of a month, and praying its nights

1331
01:41:25,048 --> 01:41:31,806
and if he dies the rewards of the deeds he used to do would continue, and his provisions would continue.

1332
01:41:32,072 --> 01:41:34,932
He would be spared the trial of the angels of the grave.

1333
01:41:35,695 --> 01:41:36,422
That's in Muslim(ألمسلم).

1334
01:41:38,327 --> 01:41:40,759
The next Hadith(حديث) is an Al-Hakim(ألحاكم) and Abu Daud(أبوداؤد).

1335
01:41:41,592 --> 01:41:44,372
Every dead person would have his deeds, sealed,

1336
01:41:45,041 --> 01:41:50,922
except the ones stationed in the path of Allah, before they would have their deeds grow until the day of judgment,

1337
01:41:51,517 --> 01:41:55,717
and they would be spared the tribulation of the angels of the grave.

1338
01:41:56,556 --> 01:41:57,595
Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) states:

1339
01:41:58,523 --> 01:42:02,906
This means that Ribat(رباط) provides the greatest rewards of all after death,

1340
01:42:04,393 --> 01:42:05,686
the Messenger of Allah says,

1341
01:42:06,100 --> 01:42:12,257
If the son of Adam(آدم) dies his deeds will terminate, except for a charity that he leaves behind,

1342
01:42:12,750 --> 01:42:17,432
knowledge that benefits, or a righteous son, that would pray for him.

1343
01:42:17,889 --> 01:42:18,208
Alright!

1344
01:42:18,532 --> 01:42:21,779
Now Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) says that the Ajr(أجْر) of Ribat(رباط) is greater.

1345
01:42:21,909 --> 01:42:22,309
How come?

1346
01:42:23,071 --> 01:42:28,674
You know the Hadith(حديث) of three will have their deeds carry on after them.

1347
01:42:29,687 --> 01:42:33,351
But the Hadith(حديث) of Ribat(رباط), let me read to you Hadith(حديث) of Ribat(رباط) again so you can compare.

1348
01:42:34,046 --> 01:42:40,137
The Hadith(حديث) of Ribat(رباط) is every dead person would have his deeds sealed, except the one stationed and the path of Allah,

1349
01:42:40,499 --> 01:42:42,996
for they would have their deeds grow until the day of judgment.

1350
01:42:44,569 --> 01:42:45,414
The other Hadith(حديث):

1351
01:42:45,482 --> 01:42:51,675
If the son of Adam(آدم) dies, his deeds would terminate except for a charity that he leaves behind, knowledge that benefits

1352
01:42:51,947 --> 01:42:53,714
our righteous son that would pray for him.

1353
01:42:54,140 --> 01:42:56,958
How come Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) considers Ribat(رباط) to be greater than these three.?

1354
01:42:58,737 --> 01:42:59,179
What is that?

1355
01:43:00,341 --> 01:43:02,626
That's not the reason, he mentions. No!

1356
01:43:07,599 --> 01:43:08,935
He hasn't mentioned that.

1357
01:43:12,327 --> 01:43:17,284
Charity, knowledge, and a righteous son would all end one day,

1358
01:43:18,828 --> 01:43:20,353
a son that you left behind is gonna die,

1359
01:43:21,169 --> 01:43:23,095
money that you leave behind is gonna run out,

1360
01:43:23,690 --> 01:43:30,629
and knowledge that you teach will be dispersed and might not be carried until the day of judgment.

1361
01:43:31,147 --> 01:43:31,787
But Ribat(رباط)!!!

1362
01:43:32,224 --> 01:43:37,004
The Hadith(حديث) says what you were doing, will carry on until the day of judgment, it is not gonna stop.

1363
01:43:39,674 --> 01:43:43,437
He says: It would end when the charity runs out.

1364
01:43:43,868 --> 01:43:47,939
When the knowledge is left, because we know the Hadith(حديث), that the time will come when knowledge will be left.

1365
01:43:48,634 --> 01:43:54,601
And when his son dies, but the rewards of the one stationed in the path of Allah continue until the Day of Judgment.

1366
01:43:55,315 --> 01:44:01,190
That is because all good deeds, cannot be practiced except when safety from the enemy is provided,

1367
01:44:01,618 --> 01:44:05,919
and that is done by the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) who are stationed, and guarding the Ummah(امة).

1368
01:44:07,863 --> 01:44:12,303
And definitely Al-Qurtubi(ألقرطبي) knows very well, what Ribat(رباط) entails,

1369
01:44:13,085 --> 01:44:15,873
because he's a scholar of Al-Andalus(ألأندلس) he's from Qurtaba(قرطبة).

1370
01:44:17,177 --> 01:44:18,902
Uthman(عثمان) stood on the pulpit and said:

1371
01:44:19,945 --> 01:44:25,064
I heard from the Messenger of Allah, a Hadith(حديث) that I didn't tell you about previously,

1372
01:44:25,768 --> 01:44:28,339
because I feared you would all leave from Madina.

1373
01:44:28,656 --> 01:44:30,233
I fear that you're gonna leave me alone.

1374
01:44:31,598 --> 01:44:39,052
I heard him say being stationed in the path of Allah for a day is better than 1000 days, anywhere else.

1375
01:44:39,623 --> 01:44:41,110
So let everyone choose what they like,

1376
01:44:42,100 --> 01:44:44,533
this is in Musanaf Ibn Abi Shaibah(مصنف إبن أبي شعيبة), At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ) and in An-Nasai(ألنسائ).

1377
01:44:45,190 --> 01:44:49,988
One day in Ribat(رباط) is like better than 1000 days, anywhere else, including Makkah and Madina.

1378
01:44:50,814 --> 01:44:53,727
Uthman(عثمان) said: I didn't tell you because I didn't want you to leave me.

1379
01:44:54,459 --> 01:44:57,680
Then he had to tell him because he didn't want to consume knowledge.

1380
01:44:58,843 --> 01:44:59,743
Ibn Nuhas(إبن نُحاس) says:

1381
01:45:00,971 --> 01:45:07,870
The Hadith(حديث) of Uthman(عثمان) is clear evidence of being stationed in the path of Allah for a day in the land of war

1382
01:45:08,449 --> 01:45:13,107
is better than spending 1000 days in any other place including Makkah, Madina and Jerusalem.

1383
01:45:14,173 --> 01:45:17,089
That is why Uthman(عثمان) didn't tell them the Hadith(حديث) before.

1384
01:45:17,528 --> 01:45:19,777
It was because, he was worried that they would all leave him.

1385
01:45:20,604 --> 01:45:26,163
The Sahabah(صحابه) and Tabieen(تابعين), whose numbers only Allah can count, who left Makkah and Madina

1386
01:45:26,493 --> 01:45:32,755
and headed to the coasts of a Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) being stationed there until they died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد), or died a natural death.

1387
01:45:36,162 --> 01:45:41,274
Al-Haris Ibn Hishaam(ألحارث بن حشام), the brother of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was leaving Makkah to Jihad(جهاد),

1388
01:45:41,840 --> 01:45:48,060
so the people of Makkah warned him, multitudes of people followed him out of Makkah, until he reached to Al-Bat'ha(ألبطحا),

1389
01:45:48,494 --> 01:45:49,843
the peoples around him cried.

1390
01:45:50,671 --> 01:45:53,168
When he saw that he himself cried and then said:

1391
01:45:53,208 --> 01:46:00,482
O people, I am not leaving you because you are not dear to me, nor am I leaving this town because I prefer some other place.

1392
01:46:01,174 --> 01:46:07,542
But this affair, started in Islam and some men went out, they were not among the most noble of us.

1393
01:46:07,988 --> 01:46:12,602
We then woke up, but in the name of Allah if the mountains of Makkah turned into gold,

1394
01:46:13,040 --> 01:46:17,706
and we spend it in the cause of Allah, we won't catch up with one day of their days.

1395
01:46:17,871 --> 01:46:22,951
Now if they are ahead of us in this world, we are going to try to catch them up in the hereafter.

1396
01:46:23,237 --> 01:46:24,259
I'm traveling to Allah.

1397
01:46:25,316 --> 01:46:28,497
He went to Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) and he died as a Shaheed(شَهِيد) in the Battle of Yarmook(يرموك).

1398
01:46:28,811 --> 01:46:35,379
He is saying that the early Muslims, received the greatest reward and there's nothing that we can do to catch up with them,

1399
01:46:36,474 --> 01:46:41,101
but we're gonna try to catch up with them using the fastest means and those fastest means were

1400
01:46:41,657 --> 01:46:43,162
Ribat(رباط) and Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

1401
01:46:44,229 --> 01:46:48,271
So this is how, you can make up for a life that you have wasted.

1402
01:46:49,490 --> 01:46:50,507
Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) said:

1403
01:46:51,206 --> 01:46:57,028
It is the consensus of all the scholars that for a man to spend time stationed in the path of Allah

1404
01:46:57,401 --> 01:47:00,081
is better than staying in Makkah and Madina or Jerusalem.

1405
01:47:01,542 --> 01:47:04,921
Ibn Mundhar(أبن ألمنذر) conveyed that that Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) was asked:

1406
01:47:05,564 --> 01:47:10,343
Which is more beloved to you, staying in Makkah, or being stationed in the path of Allah?

1407
01:47:10,427 --> 01:47:12,686
He said: Being stationed is more beloved to me.

1408
01:47:13,064 --> 01:47:14,278
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) also said:

1409
01:47:14,782 --> 01:47:18,514
Nothing is equivalent in our view to fighting and stationing in the path of Allah.

1410
01:47:19,887 --> 01:47:25,406
A man asked Imam Malik(إمام مالك), Which do you prefer for me to stay in Madina or Alexandria.?

1411
01:47:26,224 --> 01:47:29,711
He said: Stay in Alexandria, because it was a land of Ribat(رباط) at that time.

1412
01:47:30,626 --> 01:47:37,174
Also the prayer of Ribat(رباط) is multiplied, so it's fasting remembrance of Allah, Recitation of Qur'an

1413
01:47:37,548 --> 01:47:39,915
and spending the wealth in the sake of Allah,

1414
01:47:40,896 --> 01:47:42,026
In Sha Allah(إن شاءالله) we will carry on.

1415
01:47:43,292 --> 01:47:45,357
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

